{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T14:49:15.032Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<subagent_notification>\n{\"agent_path\":\"019eb1fc-186e-7cf3-aba3-4344cf8eba0f\",\"status\":{\"completed\":\"**Verdict**\\nRadar/MCP calls are authentic in newer artifacts, but there is zero proof-ready lift because no release-candidate Radar suite simultaneously has: 4/4 clean Radar validation, no-brain headroom, stable lift, and 4/4 audit-clean named-tool MCP backing.\\n\\n**Failed Suites**\\nRelease-candidate Radar failures:\\n\\n| Suite | Failure mode |\\n|---|---|\\n| `...radar-mcp-manual-attribution-20260610Tprogress` | Incomplete: 5 records, no `summary.json`; only 1 MCP run. Old log proves `brain_regressions` name but lacks `tool_args` / `tool_result`. |\\n| `...deletions-20260610Tprogress` | 0.25 -> 0.25 pass rate. Radar failed 3/4 by only partially restoring `RealignAttributionBase(newHead)` sites. Old logs not proof-complete. |\\n| `...deletions-all-loci-20260610Tprogress` | 0.50 -> 0.75, but Radar not clean. One Radar rep had no MCP call/no edit; older logs lack completed named-tool proof. |\\n| `...deletions-all-loci-rerun-20260610Tprogress` | Raw summary says 0.25 -> 1.00 and `proof_ready=true`, but audit rejects it: all condition logs are old style with no `tool_args` / `tool_result`, so audit-clean condition backing is 0/4. |\\n| `...deletions-behavior-tool-result-20260610T130500Z` | 0.75 -> 0.75. One Radar rep no-called/no-edited; only 3/4 audit-clean MCP condition records. |\\n| `...deletions-tool-result-20260610T115718Z` | 0.00 -> 0.75 with 4/4 named-tool completion, but Radar arm is 3/4 valid, so not clean. |\\n| `...deletions-tool-result-rerun-20260610T122500Z` | 0.25 -> 0.75 with 4/4 named-tool completion, but Radar arm is again 3/4 valid. |\\n| `...manual-attribution-tool-args-20260610T1415Z` | 1.00 -> 0.50, Radar worse. Calls were real but only `location_only`; current task needs deletion signals. Hidden behavior test failed in 2/4 Radar reps. |\\n| `...calibrated-*`, `...context-tool-result`, `...manual-attribution-tool-result` | Incomplete/no summary or no Radar comparison. |\\n\\nBroader existing Radar evidence: 21 Radar comparisons, 0 proof-ready; statuses were 8 `brain-not-clean`, 7 `no-brain-too-easy`, 4 `saturated`, 1 `audit-mismatch`, 1 `promotable-pilot`.\\n\\n**Harness / Reporting Gaps**\\nNo fake-call harness gap now. [run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:267) and [run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:421) cover `brain_regressions` / workspace Radar parsing and required-tool audits.\\n\\nTwo reporting gaps remain:\\n\\n1. [audit_radar_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py:60) only iterates suites with `summary.json`, so incomplete release-candidate dirs silently disappear from Radar totals.\\n\\n2. [audit_radar_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py:176) labels some cases as “summary mismatch” when the raw summary is accurate but audit-clean MCP backing was filtered away. Better label: `audit-backing-gap`.\\n\\nAlso: [audit_codex.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:223) can fall back to the current task file for `radar_include_deletions` when old records did not embed it, which can retroactively change audit flags.\\n\\n**Minimal Next Patch / Test**\\nPatch the audit/reporting first:\\n\\n- Add `incomplete-suite` rows for matching dirs with `records.ndjson` but no `summary.json`.\\n- Split raw summary consistency from audit-clean backing, with a status like `audit-backing-gap`.\\n- Require Radar policy attestation from record provenance for `radar_include_deletions`; do not silently use today’s task file for old records.\\n\\nThen rerun one narrow proof panel only: `release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions.json`, n=4, acceptance = 4/4 Radar valid, no-brain <4/4, 4/4 server `tool_args` with `location_only` and `include_deletions`, and 4/4 `tool_result ok`.\\n\\nRead-only note: I did not edit files, but the worktree currently shows dirty changes in `run_test.py`, `entireio-cli-manual-commit-attribution-base.json`, and `internal/cli/regression.go`; I left them untouched.\"}}\n</subagent_notification>"}]}}
