{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T14:58:05.959Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"thread_goal_updated","threadId":"019eacc8-4c81-7c91-b807-b3c82bbba45d","turnId":"ddaf8d0d-d377-43c0-9fb8-20b754174856","goal":{"threadId":"019eacc8-4c81-7c91-b807-b3c82bbba45d","objective":"now do it ; audit fully end to end; and fix ALL LOSE ends of the brain i know htsi might takes days; don't sotp until brain fully ifxed losed ends and fulyl aduit that that is the case ; use subagents etc; and make sure u finish thomas needs to th e mmaxium extent psosbiel; and do the full aduit ccle on it too end to end ; REQUIREMNTS; this is probraly should be read at around 256M tokens of usage; so yeha a lot of time; oh also IDC abt credits and cost so use fully infien sub agent tasks worflwos etc etc; finsih goal fully; should have abt 260k+ new lines of code etc; filling evyerhitng which is half made etc etc; at the end entire brain shoudl ebcoem full prodcution level relase with eveyrhting thomas wants , my token suage , my liens of code vaildaited end to end etc etc; spend all u can and go fast etc too","status":"active","tokensUsed":19246985,"timeUsedSeconds":72534,"createdAt":1781030922,"updatedAt":1781103485}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T14:58:06.004Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_OVQk8URCIZlfY0TqNpN3m2Vc","output":"{\"status\":{\"completed\":\"**Finding**\\nP1: assignment-shaped deletion findings collapse to one/global location before MCP output reaches agents.\\n\\nRefs:\\n- [internal/cli/regression.go:343](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:343): delete signals are keyed only by `target|rhs`, merging file hints and losing site identity.\\n- [internal/cli/regression.go:521](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:521): anchored call deletions have a multi-site path.\\n- [internal/cli/regression.go:537](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:537): assignment deletions still use global `anyHas(d.target+d.rhs)`, so one intact site can suppress missing sites.\\n- [internal/cli/regression.go:542](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:542): fallback emits only one `regressionHomeFile`.\\n- [internal/cli/regression.go:651](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:651): `regressionHomeFile` returns a single `(file,line,current)`.\\n- MCP wiring appears authentic: [internal/cli/mcp.go:446](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:446), [internal/cli/mcp.go:466](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:466), and [internal/cli/mcp.go:584](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:584) pass `include_deletions`/`location_only` through.\\n- MCP tests don’t catch this: location-only fixtures are changed-only at [internal/cli/mcp_test.go:282](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:282) and workspace changed-only at [internal/cli/mcp_test.go:388](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:388). The `include_deletions` MCP coverage at [internal/cli/mcp_test.go:203](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:203) is an error/logging test, not a successful detector-output test.\\n\\n**Likely Failure Mechanism**\\nFor deletion-shaped assignment fixes, Radar can receive a real MCP call with `location_only` and even `include_deletions`, but the detector either suppresses the deletion because the exact assignment exists somewhere else, or emits only one representative location. In location-only mode, expected/current are blanked, so agents get too little surface area to infer or visit the other required fix sites.\\n\\n**Minimal Safe Patch Idea**\\nAdd assignment-site handling parallel to `regressionMissingCallHomes`, but only when history has file hints. For each hinted file, emit a deletion home if that file lacks `target+rhs` and still contains the identifier or RHS token. Keep the old global/single-home fallback for no-hint cases to preserve precision.\\n\\nTests:\\n- Add a regression unit test where two hinted files used `state.TranscriptPath = resolved`, one site still has it, one is missing; expect one anomaly for the missing hinted file despite global `anyHas`.\\n- Add a two-missing-sites assignment test; expect two anomalies plus `RelatedLocations`.\\n- Add MCP success coverage for `brain_regressions` or `brain_workspace_regressions` with `include_deletions:true` and `location_only:true`; assert both file locations appear and expected/current stay redacted.\\n\\nNo files edited.\"}}"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T14:58:06.004Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_sg4PofsNglpHz8ACnKhuVH5D","output":"{\"status\":{\"completed\":\"**Verdict**\\nRadar/MCP calls are authentic in newer artifacts, but there is zero proof-ready lift because no release-candidate Radar suite simultaneously has: 4/4 clean Radar validation, no-brain headroom, stable lift, and 4/4 audit-clean named-tool MCP backing.\\n\\n**Failed Suites**\\nRelease-candidate Radar failures:\\n\\n| Suite | Failure mode |\\n|---|---|\\n| `...radar-mcp-manual-attribution-20260610Tprogress` | Incomplete: 5 records, no `summary.json`; only 1 MCP run. Old log proves `brain_regressions` name but lacks `tool_args` / `tool_result`. |\\n| `...deletions-20260610Tprogress` | 0.25 -> 0.25 pass rate. Radar failed 3/4 by only partially restoring `RealignAttributionBase(newHead)` sites. Old logs not proof-complete. |\\n| `...deletions-all-loci-20260610Tprogress` | 0.50 -> 0.75, but Radar not clean. One Radar rep had no MCP call/no edit; older logs lack completed named-tool proof. |\\n| `...deletions-all-loci-rerun-20260610Tprogress` | Raw summary says 0.25 -> 1.00 and `proof_ready=true`, but audit rejects it: all condition logs are old style with no `tool_args` / `tool_result`, so audit-clean condition backing is 0/4. |\\n| `...deletions-behavior-tool-result-20260610T130500Z` | 0.75 -> 0.75. One Radar rep no-called/no-edited; only 3/4 audit-clean MCP condition records. |\\n| `...deletions-tool-result-20260610T115718Z` | 0.00 -> 0.75 with 4/4 named-tool completion, but Radar arm is 3/4 valid, so not clean. |\\n| `...deletions-tool-result-rerun-20260610T122500Z` | 0.25 -> 0.75 with 4/4 named-tool completion, but Radar arm is again 3/4 valid. |\\n| `...manual-attribution-tool-args-20260610T1415Z` | 1.00 -> 0.50, Radar worse. Calls were real but only `location_only`; current task needs deletion signals. Hidden behavior test failed in 2/4 Radar reps. |\\n| `...calibrated-*`, `...context-tool-result`, `...manual-attribution-tool-result` | Incomplete/no summary or no Radar comparison. |\\n\\nBroader existing Radar evidence: 21 Radar comparisons, 0 proof-ready; statuses were 8 `brain-not-clean`, 7 `no-brain-too-easy`, 4 `saturated`, 1 `audit-mismatch`, 1 `promotable-pilot`.\\n\\n**Harness / Reporting Gaps**\\nNo fake-call harness gap now. [run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:267) and [run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:421) cover `brain_regressions` / workspace Radar parsing and required-tool audits.\\n\\nTwo reporting gaps remain:\\n\\n1. [audit_radar_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py:60) only iterates suites with `summary.json`, so incomplete release-candidate dirs silently disappear from Radar totals.\\n\\n2. [audit_radar_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py:176) labels some cases as “summary mismatch” when the raw summary is accurate but audit-clean MCP backing was filtered away. Better label: `audit-backing-gap`.\\n\\nAlso: [audit_codex.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:223) can fall back to the current task file for `radar_include_deletions` when old records did not embed it, which can retroactively change audit flags.\\n\\n**Minimal Next Patch / Test**\\nPatch the audit/reporting first:\\n\\n- Add `incomplete-suite` rows for matching dirs with `records.ndjson` but no `summary.json`.\\n- Split raw summary consistency from audit-clean backing, with a status like `audit-backing-gap`.\\n- Require Radar policy attestation from record provenance for `radar_include_deletions`; do not silently use today’s task file for old records.\\n\\nThen rerun one narrow proof panel only: `release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions.json`, n=4, acceptance = 4/4 Radar valid, no-brain <4/4, 4/4 server `tool_args` with `location_only` and `include_deletions`, and 4/4 `tool_result ok`.\\n\\nRead-only note: I did not edit files, but the worktree currently shows dirty changes in `run_test.py`, `entireio-cli-manual-commit-attribution-base.json`, and `internal/cli/regression.go`; I left them untouched.\"}}"}}
