{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:01:41.761Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_vXetJUslYU22GbzjxRmaHK1h","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb1fc-01b4-7021-a5ad-3b08ff1f2a0c\":{\"completed\":\"No P0 found. I do see one remaining P1 false-negative risk in deletion-shaped Radar.\\n\\n**P1 Finding**\\nAssignment-deletion homes can still be suppressed by a nearby/intact same-file site.\\n\\nRefs:\\n- [internal/cli/regression.go:537](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:537): hinted assignment deletions enter the new multi-home path.\\n- [internal/cli/regression.go:668](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:668): each candidate home is checked.\\n- [internal/cli/regression.go:669](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:669): presence uses a `±8` line window, not the enclosing symbol.\\n- [internal/cli/regression.go:710](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:710): candidate collection returns only target-id homes if any exist in the file, so RHS-only missing sites are never considered.\\n- [internal/cli/regression.go:552](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:552): if no hinted homes survive, a single intact assignment anywhere globally suppresses the signal.\\n\\nLikely failure mechanism:\\nIf one function in a hinted file still has `state.TranscriptPath = resolved`, and a nearby broken function deleted that assignment entirely, the intact function can mask the missing one. This is especially likely when the broken function no longer mentions `TranscriptPath` but still has `resolved`; `regressionAssignmentCandidateHomes` short-circuits before considering RHS candidates. The result is no deletion anomaly, so authentic MCP calls with `include_deletions:true` + `location_only:true` still return nothing for that missing site.\\n\\nMinimal safe fix:\\nCollect candidate homes by enclosing symbol from both `d.id` and `d.rhs`, preferring id lines when both exist. Then decide “assignment present” within that same enclosing symbol, not with a cross-symbol `±8` line window. Keep the window only as a fallback when no symbol can be inferred.\\n\\nTests to add:\\n- `regression_test.go`: same file with `ok()` containing `state.TranscriptPath = resolved` and adjacent `miss()` containing only `resolved := compute(); return resolved`; expect one deleted anomaly for `miss`.\\n- `mcp_test.go` or workspace MCP fixture: call `brain_regressions`/`brain_workspace_regressions` with `include_deletions:true, location_only:true`; assert the missing site appears and expected/current values are redacted.\\n\\nI also checked `mcp.go` include-deletions/location-only plumbing and schema validation; those paths look wired correctly. Focused tests passed:\\n\\n`go test ./internal/cli -run 'Test(MCP|Regression|Workspace.*Regression|Workspace.*Review)'`\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
