{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:06:46.840Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"thread_goal_updated","threadId":"019eacc8-4c81-7c91-b807-b3c82bbba45d","turnId":"ddaf8d0d-d377-43c0-9fb8-20b754174856","goal":{"threadId":"019eacc8-4c81-7c91-b807-b3c82bbba45d","objective":"now do it ; audit fully end to end; and fix ALL LOSE ends of the brain i know htsi might takes days; don't sotp until brain fully ifxed losed ends and fulyl aduit that that is the case ; use subagents etc; and make sure u finish thomas needs to th e mmaxium extent psosbiel; and do the full aduit ccle on it too end to end ; REQUIREMNTS; this is probraly should be read at around 256M tokens of usage; so yeha a lot of time; oh also IDC abt credits and cost so use fully infien sub agent tasks worflwos etc etc; finsih goal fully; should have abt 260k+ new lines of code etc; filling evyerhitng which is half made etc etc; at the end entire brain shoudl ebcoem full prodcution level relase with eveyrhting thomas wants , my token suage , my liens of code vaildaited end to end etc etc; spend all u can and go fast etc too","status":"active","tokensUsed":19365684,"timeUsedSeconds":73055,"createdAt":1781030922,"updatedAt":1781104006}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:06:46.922Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_N1VLLORLPDspjq2KUyScVpr6","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb1fc-186e-7cf3-aba3-4344cf8eba0f\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only audit of committed `HEAD` found **no P0** and no current doc/tool-evidence overclaim that Radar has agent-lift proof. It does have **P1 harness/reporting gaps** to fix before treating Radar/MCP agent evidence as release proof.\\n\\n**Findings**\\n\\n1. **P1: `radar:screen` can still count an audit-dirty pilot as “promotable.”**  \\n   In [audit_radar_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py:461), audit backing demotion only runs when `status[\\\"proof_ready\\\"]` is true. But [radar_status](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py:385) marks one-run headroom as `promotable-pilot`, so `pilot-radar-manual-attribution-location-screen-20260610Tprogress` is counted as promotable even though MCP backing is `0/0 clean; 1/0 attempted (wrong args)`.  \\n   Fix: demote `promotable-pilot` too when Codex audit backing exists but named/completed Radar backing is not clean, e.g. `promotable-audit-gap`, and set `promotable=False`. Add a unit test with a 1x pass-rate pilot plus dirty MCP args and assert `promotable_or_proof == 0`.\\n\\n2. **P1: committed HEAD still lets Radar deletion policy come from mutable task JSON when provenance is missing.**  \\n   In committed `HEAD`, `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:223-236` falls back from record provenance to `provenance.task.path` and reads the current task file. Then `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:441-475` uses that derived value to decide whether missing `include_deletions: true` is a flag. That can retroactively reinterpret old retained records.  \\n   Fix: always write `radar_include_deletions: bool(...)` in provenance, and make release-candidate Radar records missing the embedded policy audit-dirty/hard-failed instead of reading current task files. Test: synthetic deletion Radar record with missing embedded policy and a current task file requiring deletions should fail with a provenance-policy flag, not silently inherit the task file.\\n\\n**Failed Radar Suites**\\n\\n`HEAD` Radar screen: **25 comparisons, 0 proof-ready, 1 reported promotable, 4 saturated, 8 brain-not-clean, 5 no-brain-too-easy, 6 incomplete, 1 audit-backing-gap**.\\n\\nKey exact failures:\\n- `audit-backing-gap`: `release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-all-loci-rerun-20260610Tprogress` passed `0.25 -> 1.00`, but only `0/0 clean; 4/0 attempted (wrong args)`.\\n- `brain-not-clean`: the deletion/tool-result/manual-attribution Radar candidate suites with pass rates `0.25 -> 0.25`, `0.50 -> 0.75`, `0.75 -> 0.75`, `0.00 -> 0.75`, `0.25 -> 0.75`, and `1.00 -> 0.50`.\\n- `saturated`: attribution realign, transcript reresolve, and review-file-count pilots all had `1.00 -> 1.00`.\\n- `no-brain-too-easy`: five pilots stopped because no-brain scored `92-97`, above the `85` threshold.\\n- `incomplete-suite`: six record-only/summarization-missing suites are now surfaced instead of disappearing.\\n\\n**What Checked**\\n\\n`radar:evidence` equivalent from committed HEAD passes and is honestly scoped to `mcp_radar_tool_contract`; see [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:25). Docs also say there is no retained Radar pass-rate lift proof: [diffless_review_seam.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/diffless_review_seam.md:66), [release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:538). `radar:agent-evidence` correctly fails with “no proof-ready comparison” and is optional in [mise.toml](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:135), while `release:readiness` only includes deterministic `radar:evidence` at [mise.toml](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:292).\\n\\nNote: current worktree is dirty in `audit_codex.py`, `audit_radar_evidence.py`, `run.py`, and `run_test.py`; I did not edit them. The local diff appears to address finding 2, but this audit treated committed `HEAD` as requested.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
