{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:13:39.965Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The retained screen is doing the right thing: it refuses to bless old Radar panels that either didn’t carry the deletion-policy bit, lacked `tool_result` completion proof, were noisy, or had no-brain saturation. That’s good release hygiene, but it means the next real gap is retained benchmark evidence, not the MCP implementation itself.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
