{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:17:14.322Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<subagent_notification>\n{\"agent_path\":\"019eb218-4951-7fb1-9cac-97592b329318\",\"status\":{\"completed\":\"**Findings**\\n\\n- **P1 Unsafe workspace pairing can still scan when the registered repo key is remote but the hint resolves as `local/<hash>`.**  \\n  [workspace.go:592](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:592) treats `gh/...` vs `local/...` as “not a known mismatch,” and [workspace.go:984](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:984) only skips when `PairingUnsafe` is set. In production, a moved/replaced repo with no parseable origin can compare a `gh/org/repo` brain against an unrelated local tree.  \\n  Suggested test: `TestWorkspaceRegressionsSkipsUnverifiableRemoteKeyHint`, with a `gh/example/repo` brain, a regressed hinted tree, and `git remote get-url origin` failing or returning an unparseable remote. Assert no anomalies and an unsafe/unverifiable skip.\\n\\n- **P1 Assignment-deletion localization can collapse multiple missing sites in the same symbol shape.**  \\n  [regression.go:686](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:686) dedupes candidate homes by `regressionEnclosingSymbol`, while [regression.go:714](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:714) treats an assignment anywhere in the enclosing symbol as satisfying the invariant. [regression.go:930](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:930) also drops method receiver identity, so `(*A).Resolve` and `(*B).Resolve` both become `Resolve`. Existing tests cover different symbols, not same-name/same-symbol multi-site cases.  \\n  Suggested tests: one for two receiver methods with the same method name both missing `state.TranscriptPath = resolved`, and one for a single function with two `resolved` loci where only one has the assignment.\\n\\n- **P2 Changed-regression detection is global, so an intact peer can mask a regressed hinted file.**  \\n  `changeSignal` has no per-file hints ([regression.go:75](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:75)), history scan dedupes by id/operand only ([regression.go:333](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:333)), and `anyLineBoth` suppresses a changed finding if the invariant appears anywhere ([regression.go:447](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:447)). The emit loop then stops at the first changed site ([regression.go:486](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:486)).  \\n  Suggested tests: `TestRegressionChangedOperandReportsMissingHintedFileDespiteIntactPeer` and `TestRegressionChangedOperandReportsEachRegressedHintedFile`.\\n\\n- **P2 Workspace MCP deletion/location-only coverage is thinner than the single-repo path.**  \\n  MCP wires `include_deletions` and `location_only` for workspace tools at [mcp.go:466](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:466), and redaction happens at [workspace.go:960](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:960). But [mcp_test.go:442](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:442) only exercises workspace changed findings and `brain_workspace_regressions` location-only, not deletion opt-in or `brain_workspace_review` location-only redaction.  \\n  Suggested tests: MCP workspace regressions with `include_deletions:true, location_only:true` over missing assignment sites, and MCP workspace review with `location_only:true` asserting no expected/current detail leaks.\\n\\n- **P3 Retained Radar evidence omits an existing unsafe sessions-only test.**  \\n  `TestWorkspaceRegressionsSkipsUnsafeSessionsOnlyRepo` exists at [workspace_test.go:684](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace_test.go:684), but the required evidence list stops at `TestWorkspaceRegressionsSkipsUnsafeRepo` in [audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:58](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:58) and the manifest mirrors that at [manifest.json:66](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:66).  \\n  Suggested test/evidence change: add the existing sessions-only unsafe test to `REQUIRED_TESTS` and the retained artifact command.\\n\\nI stayed read-only/offline and did not rerun `mise run radar:evidence`, since that would refresh report artifacts.\"}}\n</subagent_notification>"}]}}
