{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:28:14.465Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Quick status: for the Radar/MCP priority slice, I’d call it about **75-80% done**. The deterministic tool contract is stronger and green; what remains is full validation/commit, then a clean rerun of the Radar agent panel to see if we can get real agent-lift proof.\n\nFor the huge “entire production release with everything Thomas wants” goal, it’s still much lower, roughly **35-45% overall**, because facts-vs-raw positive proof and retained Radar agent-lift proof are still not achieved. Distill evidence, generic MCP evidence, and Radar tool-contract evidence are in much better shape.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:28:14.469Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Quick status: for the Radar/MCP priority slice, I’d call it about **75-80% done**. The deterministic tool contract is stronger and green; what remains is full validation/commit, then a clean rerun of the Radar agent panel to see if we can get real agent-lift proof.\n\nFor the huge “entire production release with everything Thomas wants” goal, it’s still much lower, roughly **35-45% overall**, because facts-vs-raw positive proof and retained Radar agent-lift proof are still not achieved. Distill evidence, generic MCP evidence, and Radar tool-contract evidence are in much better shape."}],"phase":"commentary"}}
