{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:46:11.334Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Short estimate: the **current Radar/MCP proof slice** is probably **20-25% left** if we find a clean non-saturated panel soon, but **1-3 hours** could become **longer** because agent benchmark runs are stochastic and some lanes keep turning out too easy. The bigger “all Thomas asks production-ready” goal is still much larger, roughly **55-65% left** in honest release-readiness terms.\n\nAnd yes, I can speed this up with subagents. The part they help most with is parallel audit and candidate discovery: one can hunt harder Radar tasks, one can audit MCP evidence gates, one can inspect retained release evidence, while I run/validate the best benchmark lane. The slow bit that does not parallelize cleanly is a single proof matrix, but we can run multiple candidate screens in parallel and kill saturated ones early.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:46:11.341Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Short estimate: the **current Radar/MCP proof slice** is probably **20-25% left** if we find a clean non-saturated panel soon, but **1-3 hours** could become **longer** because agent benchmark runs are stochastic and some lanes keep turning out too easy. The bigger “all Thomas asks production-ready” goal is still much larger, roughly **55-65% left** in honest release-readiness terms.\n\nAnd yes, I can speed this up with subagents. The part they help most with is parallel audit and candidate discovery: one can hunt harder Radar tasks, one can audit MCP evidence gates, one can inspect retained release evidence, while I run/validate the best benchmark lane. The slow bit that does not parallelize cleanly is a single proof matrix, but we can run multiple candidate screens in parallel and kill saturated ones early."}],"phase":"commentary"}}
