{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:47:26.314Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_dZ0crlec7x4tgv1mdQPKuzFi","output":"Chunk ID: 676eb5\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 1224\nOutput:\n\n--- entireio-cli-radar-attribution-realign-state.json\nid : entireio-cli-radar-attribution-realign-state\nrepo : entire-cli\nrepo_path : cli-bench\nconditions : ['no_brain', 'mcp_history']\nprompt : Fix the attribution realignment regression. When session attribution is brought back into sync with a new base, future attribution must diff against that new base and stale divergence-warning bookkeeping must be cleared.\nradar_include_deletions : True\nworkspace_name : None\nvalidation : [\"test $(rg -n 's\\\\.AttributionBaseCommit = newBase' cmd/entire/cli/session/state.go | wc -l | tr -d ' ') -eq 1\", 'go test ./cmd/entire/cli/session -run TestState_RealignAttributionBase_ClearsDivergenceFlag']\nexpected_files : ['cmd/entire/cli/session/state.go']\nbrain_queries : ['RealignAttributionBase', 'AttributionBaseCommit', 'DivergenceNoticeShown', 'newBase']\n\n--- entireio-cli-radar-review-base-file-count.json\nid : entireio-cli-radar-review-base-file-count\nrepo : entire-cli\nrepo_path : cli-bench\nconditions : ['no_brain', 'mcp_history']\nprompt : Fix the review banner regression for stacked branch reviews: when an explicit base branch is supplied and the default branch has moved independently, one of the banner's scope counts is computed against the wrong comparison point. The base label is already correct. Keep the fix minimal.\nradar_include_deletions : None\nworkspace_name : None\nvalidation : ['test $(rg -n \\'baseRef\\\\+\"\\\\.\\\\.\\\\.HEAD\"\\' cmd/entire/cli/review/scope.go | wc -l | tr -d \\' \\') -eq 1', 'python3 - <<\\'PY\\'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nPath(\\'cmd/entire/cli/review/scope_radar_hidden_test.go\\').write_text(r\\'\\'\\'package review\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\"context\"\\n\\t\"os/exec\"\\n\\t\"testing\"\\n)\\n\\nfunc TestComputeScopeStats_BaseOverrideFileCountUsesOverride(t *testing.T) {\\n\\tdir := t.TempDir()\\n\\tinitRepoOnMain(t, dir)\\n\\tcommitFile(t, dir, \"root.go\", \"package main\", \"init\")\\n\\n\\trun := func(args ...string) {\\n\\t\\tt.Helper()\\n\\t\\tcmd := exec.Command(\"git\", args...)\\n\\t\\tcmd.Dir = dir\\n\\t\\tif out, err := cmd.CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\"git %v: %v\\\\n%s\", args, err, out)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\trun(\"checkout\", \"-b\", \"feat/parent\")\\n\\tcommitFile(t, dir, \"parent.go\", \"package main\", \"parent\")\\n\\trun(\"checkout\", \"-b\", \"feat/child\")\\n\\tcommitFile(t, dir, \"child.go\", \"package main\", \"child\")\\n\\trun(\"checkout\", \"main\")\\n\\tcommitFile(t, dir, \"main_only.go\", \"package main\", \"main only\")\\n\\trun(\"checkout\", \"feat/child\")\\n\\n\\tstats, err := ComputeScopeStats(context.Background(), openTestRepo(t, dir), \"feat/parent\")\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\tt.Fatal(err)\\n\\t}\\n\\tif stats.FilesChanged != 1 {\\n\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\"FilesChanged = %d, want 1; explicit base must not use main...HEAD\", stats.FilesChanged)\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\\'\\'\\')\\nPY\\nrc=0\\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/review -run \\'^TestComputeScopeStats_BaseOverrideFileCountUsesOverride$\\' -count=1 || rc=$?\\nrm -f cmd/entire/cli/review/scope_radar_hidden_test.go\\nexit $rc']\nexpected_files : ['cmd/entire/cli/review/scope.go']\nbrain_queries : ['countFilesChanged', 'baseRef', 'FilesChanged', 'three-dot diff']\n\n--- entireio-cli-review-base-flag-scope.json\nid : entireio-cli-review-base-flag-scope\nrepo : entire-cli\nrepo_path : cli-bench\nconditions : ['no_brain', 'full_cli_compact', 'mcp_history']\nprompt : Fix the review scope regression: `entire review --base <ref>` must use the explicit base ref when collecting checkpoint context and composing the agent prompt/banner. Preserve the existing review checkpoint context behavior.\nradar_include_deletions : None\nworkspace_name : None\nvalidation : ['test $(rg -n \\'scopeBaseRef\\\\+\"\\\\.\\\\.HEAD\"\\' cmd/entire/cli/review_context.go | wc -l | tr -d \\' \\') -eq 1', \"go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestReviewCommandSmoke_BaseFlagThreadsThroughToPromptAndBanner|REDACTED'\"]\nexpected_files : ['cmd/entire/cli/review_context.go']\nbrain_queries : ['reviewContextCommitMessages', 'scopeBaseRef', 'BaseFlagThreadsThroughToPromptAndBanner']\n\n--- entireio-cli-manual-commit-attribution-base.json\nid : entireio-cli-manual-commit-attribution-base\nrepo : entire-cli\nrepo_path : cli-bench\nconditions : ['no_brain', 'full_cli_compact', 'mcp_history']\nprompt : Fix the release-candidate stale-session-state regression. A hidden integration shows that after an ordinary commit during an active session, later accounting remains anchored to stale state. Keep the fix minimal.\nradar_include_deletions : True\nworkspace_name : None\nvalidation : [\"go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'TestPostCommit_NoTrailer_UpdatesBaseCommit|TestPostCommitNoTrailerRealignsAttributionBaseHidden' -count=1\"]\nexpected_files : ['cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go']\nbrain_queries : ['AttributionBaseCommit stale human_added no trailer', 'TestManualCommit_AttributionStaleBase', 'BaseCommit AttributionBaseCommit realign', 'RealignAttributionBase newHead manual commit hooks']\n"}}
