{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:49:42.221Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_dHfHecltILJxrXbiqXXm4SIj","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb1c9-da6e-7553-a01e-d6837efa84a3\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only audit complete. No files edited, no PR/push.\\n\\n**Findings**\\n\\n1. [internal/cli/workspace_test.go:556](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace_test.go:556) covers workspace `regressions` only for a changed-shape finding. The detector has strong direct coverage for same-file deletion multi-locus at [internal/cli/regression_test.go:346](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression_test.go:346), and single-repo MCP covers it at [internal/cli/mcp_test.go:304](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:304), but the cross-repo release path lacks a two-site deletion test.  \\nSmallest fix: add a workspace regressions JSON test with `--include-deletions --location-only`, one repo, `missOne`/`missTwo`, and assert both symbols plus `related_locations` survive while `Expected`/`Current` are blank.\\n\\n2. [internal/cli/mcp_test.go:473](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:473) tests `brain_workspace_regressions` deletion redaction, but only with one missing locus. That leaves the MCP benchmark path under-tested for same-file multi-locus guidance emitted by [internal/cli/workspace.go:955](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:955).  \\nSmallest fix: extend this fixture to include `ok`, `missOne`, and `missTwo`; assert both missing symbols and `related_locations` appear in the MCP JSON, and the expected assignment/current line do not.\\n\\n3. [internal/cli/mcp_test.go:200](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:200) verifies MCP debug logging for an error result only. Since benchmark evidence often needs proof that the named tool actually completed, [internal/cli/mcp.go:159](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:159) should have a success-path test too.  \\nSmallest fix: add a valid `brain_workspace_regressions` call with `include_deletions:true` and `location_only:true`; assert the log contains `tool_result: brain_workspace_regressions ok`, safe boolean args, and no query/expected/current leakage.\\n\\n4. [internal/cli/regression.go:1041](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:1041) groups `RelatedLocations` by same file + same kind only. If two unrelated deleted invariants land in one file, location-only output may tell agents to inspect unrelated same-file locations.  \\nSmallest detector tweak: when adding related locations, also require matching `Identifier` or matching despaced `Expected`. Focused test: two deletion invariants in one file, only one with two missing sites; assert related locations do not cross-contaminate.\\n\\n5. [internal/cli/regression.go:179](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:179) and [internal/cli/regression.go:180](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:180) extract deletion signals with narrow RHS/call regexes. This is fine for current fixtures, but multi-arg helper calls or function-call RHS values are likely benchmark-evasion shapes.  \\nSmallest test first: add extraction tests for `state.TranscriptPath = agent.ResolveSessionFile(sessionDir, agentSessionID)` and `state.RealignAttributionBase(newHead, reason)`. If they fail, broaden extraction to keep the callee/first discriminative argument instead of dropping the signal.\\n\\nNet: I’d prioritize the workspace MCP multi-locus test plus success debug-log test first. The detector itself has decent deletion/multi-locus coverage; the release-readiness gap is proving that behavior through the actual cross-repo MCP benchmark surface.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
