{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:56:10.533Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_nGTMqfUQhwcb8rqdHoFwbdm0","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb218-2e2a-7a82-9d0c-49f4e4597681\":{\"completed\":\"**Current State**\\nI kept this read-only: no edits, no network, no PR/push. Current retained gates:\\n\\n`mise run release:evidence` passes for generic replay-lab evidence: 2 suites, 16 records, 0 hard flags, proof scopes `history` and `mcp`.\\n\\n`mise run radar:evidence` passes for deterministic MCP/Radar tool-contract evidence: 44 required tests.\\n\\n`mise run radar:agent-evidence` fails as expected: no retained proof-ready Regression Radar agent comparison.\\n\\nKey policy files:\\n[manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json:1)\\n[release README](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/README.md:1)\\n[mise.toml](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:22)\\n\\n**Fresh Suite To Retained Evidence**\\n1. Run a committed release panel into `benchmarks/agent-brain/results`:\\n\\n```sh\\nsuite=\\\"release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)\\\"\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py panel release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions \\\\\\n  --suite-name \\\"$suite\\\" \\\\\\n  --pricing-file benchmarks/agent-brain/pricing.json\\n```\\n\\nFor workspace Radar, use `release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve`. For generic MCP, use `release-entire-cli-mcp-manual-attribution`.\\n\\n2. Pre-audit before retention:\\n\\n```sh\\ntmp=\\\"$(mktemp -d)\\\"\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py \\\\\\n  --results benchmarks/agent-brain/results \\\\\\n  --suite-glob \\\"$suite\\\" \\\\\\n  --out-dir \\\"$tmp\\\" \\\\\\n  --fail-on-flags \\\\\\n  --min-suites 1 \\\\\\n  --min-records 8 \\\\\\n  --min-proof-ready 1 \\\\\\n  --min-mcp-verified 4 \\\\\\n  --min-mcp-named-tool-verified 4\\n\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py \\\\\\n  --results benchmarks/agent-brain/results \\\\\\n  --suite-glob \\\"$suite\\\" \\\\\\n  --out-dir \\\"$tmp\\\" \\\\\\n  --codex-audit-report \\\"$tmp/codex-audit-report.json\\\" \\\\\\n  --fail-when-no-proof\\n```\\n\\nRadar proof must be stable, n>=4 per side, no-brain pass rate <1.0, Radar pass rate 1.0, and audit-backed. That logic is in [audit_radar_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py:352).\\n\\n3. Copy only retained evidence into `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/$suite`:\\n\\n```sh\\ndest=\\\"benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/$suite\\\"\\nsrc=\\\"benchmarks/agent-brain/results/$suite\\\"\\nmkdir -p \\\"$dest\\\"\\ncp \\\"$src/summary.json\\\" \\\"$src/records.ndjson\\\" \\\"$dest/\\\"\\nfor d in \\\"$src\\\"/*__*; do\\n  mkdir -p \\\"$dest/${d##*/}\\\"\\n  cp \\\"$d/record.json\\\" \\\"$dest/${d##*/}/\\\"\\n  [ -f \\\"$d/mcp-server.log\\\" ] && cp \\\"$d/mcp-server.log\\\" \\\"$dest/${d##*/}/\\\"\\ndone\\n```\\n\\nFor MCP/Radar, keep `mcp-server.log`; the audit needs server-side call/name/arg/result backing.\\n\\n4. Update [evidence/release/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json:6). For one added 4x4 Radar suite, bump roughly:\\n\\n```json\\n\\\"minimums\\\": {\\n  \\\"suites\\\": 3,\\n  \\\"records\\\": 24,\\n  \\\"proof_ready_comparisons\\\": 3,\\n  \\\"mcp_verified_records\\\": 8,\\n  \\\"mcp_named_tool_verified_records\\\": 4,\\n  \\\"hard_flags\\\": 0\\n},\\n\\\"required_proof_scopes\\\": [\\\"history\\\", \\\"mcp\\\", \\\"mcp_radar_location_only\\\"],\\n\\\"required_named_tool_proof_scopes\\\": [\\\"mcp_radar_location_only\\\"]\\n```\\n\\nUse `mcp_workspace_radar_location_only` instead for workspace Radar.\\n\\n5. Regenerate retained reports and verify:\\n\\n```sh\\nmise run release:evidence:update\\nmise run release:evidence\\nmise run radar:agent-evidence\\nmise run radar:evidence\\nmise run radar:screen\\n```\\n\\n**Files That Must Change**\\nFor retained Radar agent proof:\\n\\n`benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/$suite/**`\\n`benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json`\\n`benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/codex-audit-report.json`\\n`benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/codex-audit-report.md`\\n`benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/README.md`\\n\\nUsually also update:\\n`docs/release_readiness_audit.md`\\n`docs/diffless_review_seam.md`\\n\\nFor deterministic Radar tool-contract refresh:\\n`benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/go-test-internal-cli-radar.jsonl`\\n`benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json`\\n`benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/radar-tool-audit-report.{json,md}`\\n\\n**Non-Citable Traps**\\n- Suite is only under `benchmarks/agent-brain/results`; that is quarantine, not release evidence.\\n- Suite name is not `release-candidate-*`, or is `release-local-*`.\\n- Missing `run_config.panel` provenance from a committed panel.\\n- Manifest minimums/scopes are not updated, especially Radar scope.\\n- Radar record lacks embedded `provenance.task.radar_include_deletions`; audit does not infer it from task JSON.\\n- `mcp-server.log` lacks `tool:`, safe `tool_args`, or `tool_result` lines for Radar.\\n- Radar arm is not 4/4 valid, no-brain is 4/4 saturated, n<4, or stability is noisy.\\n- `summary.json` does not match audited record counts/pass rates.\\n- Hidden validation lacks leak markers, or task exposes `benchmarks/agent-brain`.\\n- Deterministic `radar:evidence` is cited as agent pass-rate proof. It is tool-contract proof only.\"},\"019eb22a-8e82-7b11-a8f6-daf7ad5e5db4\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only audit complete. No edits, no network, no push/PR.\\n\\n**Findings**\\n\\n1. **Live `record.ok` can go green before server-log `tool_result` evidence exists.**  \\n   In [run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2998), `mcp_condition_audit` reads agent activity only; [run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:3005) sets `record.ok` without checking `mcp-server.log`. Concrete local evidence: [records.ndjson](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-20260610Tprogress/records.ndjson:8) has `ok=True`, `mcp_condition_audit.ok=True`, and `include_deletions/location_only` in activity, but the server log only has `tools/call`, `tool: brain_regressions`, and `response` at [mcp-server.log](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-20260610Tprogress/entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions__codex-gpt-5.4-mini-low__mcp_history__r4/mcp-server.log:7), with no `tool_args:` or `tool_result:`.  \\n   Suggested fix/test: add a live `mcp_server_audit` into `run_one` and require, for Radar records, one required tool call with required args and `tool_result ok` before `record.ok` can be true.\\n\\n2. **`audit_codex` separates args from successful results, so mixed calls can be merged into a false success.**  \\n   [audit_codex.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:114) records `tool_args` by current tool, while [audit_codex.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:103) records `tool_result` as tool/status only. Later, [audit_codex.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:166) accepts any args match, and [audit_codex.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:474) accepts any successful result for the same tool name. That can pass if call A had `location_only/include_deletions` but errored, and call B succeeded without those args.  \\n   Suggested fix/test: parse server logs into per-call records `{tool,args,status}` or add call IDs in [mcp.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:153). Add audit tests for mixed failed/success calls for both `brain_regressions` and `brain_workspace_regressions`.\\n\\n3. **Checked-in release gate currently passes with zero named Radar tool evidence.**  \\n   The release manifest requires only `history` and generic `mcp` proof scopes, with no named-tool proof scopes: [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json:20), [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json:24). The retained audit report passes while `mcp_named_tool_verified_records` and `mcp_named_tool_completed_records` are both `0`: [codex-audit-report.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/codex-audit-report.json:800), [codex-audit-report.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/codex-audit-report.json:832).  \\n   Suggested fix/test: for Radar release readiness, require `mcp_radar_location_only` and/or `mcp_workspace_radar_location_only` in both `required_proof_scopes` and `required_named_tool_proof_scopes`, and set named-tool minimums above zero.\\n\\n4. **Radar “exactly once/no extra MCP” is prompt-only, not enforced.**  \\n   The prompts require exact single Radar calls at [run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2054) and [run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2058), but [mcp_condition_audit](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:1207) only checks required tool presence/args. The local r4 record shows two `brain_regressions` calls yet `mcp_condition_audit.ok=True`.  \\n   Suggested fix/test: for release Radar scopes, fail on repeated required calls and any non-required MCP tool, or mark fallback `brain_brief` as a separate non-release-citable scope.\\n\\n5. **`audit_radar_evidence` can still produce summary-only Radar readiness unless invoked in the strict mode.**  \\n   The codex audit is optional at [audit_radar_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py:420); backing is enforced only when supplied at [audit_radar_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py:441), and the no-audit hard fail only applies to `--fail-when-no-proof` at [audit_radar_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py:618).  \\n   Suggested fix/test: make release-candidate Radar rows demote to `audit-missing` unless `--codex-audit-report` is supplied, including `--fail-when-no-promotable`.\"},\"019eb218-4951-7fb1-9cac-97592b329318\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only audit only: no edits, no push/PR, no benchmark runs. The strict path is wired through `mcp_history + BENCH_RADAR_LOCATION_ONLY=1` or `mcp_workspace_radar`, with audit checks for `location_only`, deletion flags, named tool logs, and `tool_result` backing in [run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:3389) and [audit_codex.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:448).\\n\\n**Top 3**\\n\\n1. `entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions`  \\nRunner/conditions: `codex:gpt-5.4-mini:low`, `no_brain,mcp_history`  \\nWhy: best release candidate. It is deletion-shaped, multi-site assignment repair, and the committed panel already forces location-only Radar via `BENCH_RADAR_LOCATION_ONLY=1` [panel](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions.json:11). The task declares `radar_include_deletions: true` and removes both `RealignAttributionBase(newHead)` sites [task](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions.json:13). Baseline still has headroom: prior strict tool-result runs were `0.0 -> 0.75` and `0.25 -> 0.75`, while an older all-loci run reached `0.25 -> 1.0` but lacked the current strict evidence shape [summary](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-tool-result-20260610T115718Z/summary.json:64).  \\nStrict MCP audit: yes, if rerun now and audit passes. Requires `brain_regressions`, `location_only:true`, `include_deletions:true`, and `tool_result: brain_regressions ok`.\\n\\n```bash\\nSUITE=release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-tool-result-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py panel release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions --suite-name \\\"$SUITE\\\"\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py --results benchmarks/agent-brain/results --suite-glob \\\"$SUITE\\\" --out-dir /tmp/radar-codex-audit --fail-on-flags --min-suites 1 --min-records 8 --min-proof-ready 1 --min-mcp-verified 4 --min-mcp-named-tool-verified 4 --min-repetitions-per-side 4\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py --results benchmarks/agent-brain/results --suite-glob \\\"$SUITE\\\" --codex-audit-report /tmp/radar-codex-audit/codex-audit-report.json --out-dir /tmp/radar-evidence-audit --fail-when-no-proof\\n```\\n\\n2. `entireio-cli-transcript-reresolve` workspace Radar  \\nRunner/conditions: `claude:haiku:xhigh`, `no_brain,mcp_workspace_radar`  \\nWhy: best committed `brain_workspace_regressions` exercise. The panel explicitly uses workspace Radar on a harder runner [panel](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve-haiku-xhigh.json:2), and the task is deletion-shaped with `workspace_name: release-radar` [task](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entireio-cli-transcript-reresolve.json:15). Historical haiku-xhigh baseline has score headroom, with `63.33` no-brain mean in prior transcript proof summaries [summary](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/cliproof-tr-claude-haiku-xhigh/summary.json:20).  \\nStrict MCP audit: yes, if it reaches the MCP arm. Requires `brain_workspace_regressions`, `workspace`, `location_only:true`, `include_deletions:true`, and `tool_result: brain_workspace_regressions ok`.\\n\\n```bash\\nSUITE=release-candidate-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve-haiku-xhigh-tool-result-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py panel release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve-haiku-xhigh --suite-name \\\"$SUITE\\\" --stop-after-no-brain-score 90\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py --results benchmarks/agent-brain/results --suite-glob \\\"$SUITE\\\" --out-dir /tmp/workspace-radar-codex-audit --fail-on-flags --min-suites 1 --min-records 8 --min-proof-ready 1 --min-mcp-verified 4 --min-mcp-named-tool-verified 4 --min-repetitions-per-side 4\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_evidence.py --results benchmarks/agent-brain/results --suite-glob \\\"$SUITE\\\" --codex-audit-report /tmp/workspace-radar-codex-audit/codex-audit-report.json --out-dir /tmp/workspace-radar-evidence-audit --fail-when-no-proof\\n```\\n\\n3. `entireio-cli-manual-commit-attribution-base` low-effort screen/proof  \\nRunner/conditions: `codex:gpt-5.4-mini:low`, `no_brain,mcp_history`  \\nWhy: lower confidence than #1, but still useful as a harder deletion-shaped Radar candidate. It declares `radar_include_deletions:true` [task](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entireio-cli-manual-commit-attribution-base.json:14), and a low-runner screen had no-brain `0.0` pass rate / score `72.0`, so baseline headroom exists [summary](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/pilot-radar-manual-attribution-low-location-screen-20260610Tprogress/summary.json:26). Caveat: one later medium strict run was brain-negative, so treat this as screen-first unless #1 gets noisy.  \\nStrict MCP audit: yes, with the env flag. Requires `brain_regressions`, `location_only:true`, `include_deletions:true`, and `tool_result`.\\n\\n```bash\\nSUITE=screen-radar-manual-attribution-base-low-tool-result-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)\\nBENCH_RADAR_LOCATION_ONLY=1 python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py run --tasks entireio-cli-manual-commit-attribution-base.json --runners codex:gpt-5.4-mini:low --conditions no_brain,mcp_history --repetitions 4 --stop-after-no-brain-score 90 --suite-name \\\"$SUITE\\\"\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py --results benchmarks/agent-brain/results --suite-glob \\\"$SUITE\\\" --out-dir /tmp/manual-base-codex-audit --fail-on-flags --min-suites 1 --min-records 8 --min-proof-ready 1 --min-mcp-verified 4 --min-mcp-named-tool-verified 4 --min-repetitions-per-side 4\\n```\\n\\nI would skip `review-base-file-count`, `attribution-realign-state`, and current `codex` transcript Radar lanes for release evidence right now: their no-brain baselines are mostly saturated or too easy. I also found no committed unsafe-repo-specific Radar/MCP benchmark task, so that remains a coverage gap rather than a runnable candidate.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
