{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T16:05:12.422Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_5mdvLjr4aUYEmNBiAIwYq7XE","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb1c9-da6e-7553-a01e-d6837efa84a3\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only audit done on `codex/release-readiness-hardening` at `caf5d36`. No edits, no PR/push.\\n\\n**Highest Gaps**\\n\\n1. [benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:267](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:267) treats `mcp_radar_answer_assisted` as requiring `brain_regressions` but no required args, so a `location_only:true` call can satisfy answer-assisted named-tool completion. That blurs the “answer-assisted” proof scope.  \\nSmallest test: add a `BENCH_REGRESSION_RADAR=1` record whose server log has `tool_args: {\\\"location_only\\\":true}` and `tool_result: brain_regressions ok`; assert it is flagged or not counted as `mcp_radar_answer_assisted` completed proof.\\n\\n2. [internal/cli/mcp.go:132](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:132) and [benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2410](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2410) only preserve boolean args. Good for redaction, but workspace Radar proof cannot verify the requested `workspace` name. A successful call to the wrong workspace would still satisfy [audit_codex.py:269](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:269).  \\nSmallest fix/test: allowlist the benchmark workspace name as a safe string for `brain_workspace_regressions`, then add an audit test where server log says `workspace:\\\"wrong\\\"` and assert `B:mcp_workspace_radar_wrong_workspace`.\\n\\n3. [benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:162](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:162) silently filters unsafe `tool_args` keys instead of flagging raw log leakage. If a future server logs `query`, the audit report hides it but the evidence artifact still leaked.  \\nSmallest test: write `mcp-server.log` with `tool_args: {\\\"query\\\":\\\"secret\\\",\\\"location_only\\\":true}` and assert an audit flag like `E:mcp_server_log_unsafe_tool_args`.\\n\\n4. [benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2362](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2362) covers the mixed-call “args on error, ok later without args” loophole for `brain_regressions`, but not `brain_workspace_regressions`. The parser is generic, but the workspace condition has separate audit branches at [audit_codex.py:508](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:508).  \\nSmallest test: same mixed-call fixture using `_workspace_mcp_release_record`, deletion policy true, first workspace call `include_deletions/location_only` + error, second workspace call ok without args; assert `B:mcp_required_tool_results_not_ok(brain_workspace_regressions)`.\\n\\n5. [internal/cli/mcp_test.go:223](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:223) tests successful debug logging only for `brain_workspace_regressions`; [internal/cli/mcp_test.go:200](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:200) tests error logging only for `brain_regressions`. Review tools are schema-visible and redaction-tested in output, but not debug-log-tested.  \\nSmallest test: table-test `brain_review` and `brain_workspace_review` with secret query plus `include_deletions/location_only`; assert debug log has `tool_result: ... ok`, safe bool args only, and no query/current/expected leak.\\n\\nNet: `caf5d36` closes the main same-call success loophole for single-repo Radar. The remaining release-readiness risk is proving the call was the right Radar mode and, for workspace Radar, the right workspace, while keeping query redaction intact.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
