{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T16:09:03.345Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_Fy3qnRS7CKfydtpcyIIbiBVP","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb15c-ebdd-7010-8d01-d3308a5d263e\":{\"completed\":\"**Ranked Gaps**\\n1. **Radar tool evidence is stale against current HEAD.**  \\n   `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json` records `source_head=209e570...` at [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:80), while `git rev-parse HEAD` is `caf5d360...`. `git show --stat --name-only HEAD` shows this commit touched Radar/MCP runtime/tests. The auditor only checks that `source_head` is 40 hex chars at [audit_radar_tool_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:129), so `mise run radar:evidence` still passes.\\n\\n2. **No retained Radar agent-lift proof.**  \\n   `mise run radar:screen` reports 26 Radar comparisons, **0 proof-ready**, **0 promotable**. `mise run radar:agent-evidence` fails with “Radar evidence has no proof-ready comparison.” But `release:readiness` runs `radar:evidence`, not `radar:agent-evidence`, at [mise.toml](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:292). Docs correctly say tool-contract only at [radar-tool-audit-report.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/radar-tool-audit-report.md:11).\\n\\n3. **Generic MCP replay proof lacks named-tool / `tool_result` proof.**  \\n   Release manifest allows `mcp_named_tool_verified_records: 0` at [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json:11) and no named-tool scopes at [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json:24). The committed report passes with named/completed counts both zero at [codex-audit-report.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/codex-audit-report.json:801). `mise run release:evidence` passes, so claims must stay generic MCP-history only.\\n\\n4. **Full release-readiness currently fails on semantic freshness.**  \\n   `mise run semantic:evidence` exits 1: `freshness=unsafe`, `head: stale`, indexed `4856a879...` vs current `caf5d360...`. This task is included in `release:readiness` at [mise.toml](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:292). Lower priority per your instruction, but it blocks the full gate.\\n\\n5. **Non-Radar public claims remain intentionally narrow.**  \\n   `mise run facts:evidence` passes only `claim_policy=no_release_claim`, `claimable_facts_vs_raw=false` at [facts-eval-audit-report.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/facts-eval-audit-report.json:6). `mise run distill:evidence` passes current-repo command-agent scheduler proof, not target large-repo/frontend proof; docs still list target artifacts as pending at [release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:584).\\n\\nNo edits made by me. Note: the worktree now shows an uncommitted `docs/release_readiness_audit.md` count change (`44` -> `47` tests); I treated it as external and did not touch it.\"},\"019eb1c9-d797-73e1-a3cb-cd83ff65795d\":{\"completed\":\"I inspected the benchmark configs/results and did not edit files.\\n\\n**Best Lanes**\\n\\n1. **Manual attribution deletions, Codex mini low, Radar location-only**\\n   - Task: `benchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions.json`\\n   - Runner/conditions: `codex:gpt-5.4-mini:low` + `no_brain,mcp_history`\\n   - Why: strongest existing non-saturated Radar signal: historical rerun showed no-brain `1/4` vs Radar `4/4`, with deletion loci included.\\n   - One-rep screen:\\n     ```sh\\n     BENCH_RADAR_LOCATION_ONLY=1 python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py run \\\\\\n       --tasks entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions.json \\\\\\n       --runners codex:gpt-5.4-mini:low \\\\\\n       --conditions no_brain,mcp_history \\\\\\n       --repetitions 1 \\\\\\n       --stop-after-no-brain-score 88 \\\\\\n       --suite-name screen-radar-manual-attribution-deletions-low-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%MZ) \\\\\\n       --timeout 1800\\n     ```\\n   - Promote if: no-brain fails validation or scores `<=85`, and Radar passes with score `>=90`, with `brain_regressions` called using `location_only=true` and `include_deletions=true`.\\n\\n2. **Transcript re-resolve, Claude Haiku xhigh, workspace Radar**\\n   - Task: `benchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entireio-cli-transcript-reresolve.json`\\n   - Runner/conditions: `claude:haiku:xhigh` + `no_brain,mcp_workspace_radar`\\n   - Why: prior generic MCP runs had real no-brain instability, while workspace Radar should give only the relocation/file signal. A previous screen was cut off at no-brain score `89` by an overly strict `85` gate.\\n   - One-rep screen:\\n     ```sh\\n     python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py run \\\\\\n       --tasks entireio-cli-transcript-reresolve.json \\\\\\n       --runners claude:haiku:xhigh \\\\\\n       --conditions no_brain,mcp_workspace_radar \\\\\\n       --repetitions 1 \\\\\\n       --stop-after-no-brain-score 90 \\\\\\n       --suite-name screen-workspace-radar-transcript-haiku-xhigh-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%MZ) \\\\\\n       --timeout 1800\\n     ```\\n   - Promote if: no-brain fails validation or scores `<=85`, and workspace Radar passes with score `>=90`. Discard if no-brain passes cleanly above `90`.\\n\\n3. **Transcript re-resolve, Claude Haiku medium, workspace Radar**\\n   - Same task, runner `claude:haiku:medium`.\\n   - Why: secondary screen for the same fair lane; historical no-brain was not saturated, MCP arm looked stable.\\n   - One-rep screen:\\n     ```sh\\n     python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py run \\\\\\n       --tasks entireio-cli-transcript-reresolve.json \\\\\\n       --runners claude:haiku:medium \\\\\\n       --conditions no_brain,mcp_workspace_radar \\\\\\n       --repetitions 1 \\\\\\n       --stop-after-no-brain-score 88 \\\\\\n       --suite-name screen-workspace-radar-transcript-haiku-medium-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%MZ) \\\\\\n       --timeout 1800\\n     ```\\n   - Promote if: no-brain fails validation or scores `<=85`, and Radar passes with score `>=90`.\\n\\n4. **Review base flag scope, Codex mini medium, Radar location-only**\\n   - Task: `benchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entireio-cli-review-base-flag-scope.json`\\n   - Runner/conditions: `codex:gpt-5.4-mini:medium` + `no_brain,mcp_history`\\n   - Why: older generic MCP proof had no-brain `5/8` vs MCP `8/8`, but recent dedicated Radar screens saturated. Treat as fallback only.\\n   - One-rep screen:\\n     ```sh\\n     BENCH_RADAR_LOCATION_ONLY=1 python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py run \\\\\\n       --tasks entireio-cli-review-base-flag-scope.json \\\\\\n       --runners codex:gpt-5.4-mini:medium \\\\\\n       --conditions no_brain,mcp_history \\\\\\n       --repetitions 1 \\\\\\n       --stop-after-no-brain-score 90 \\\\\\n       --suite-name screen-radar-review-base-scope-mini-medium-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%MZ) \\\\\\n       --timeout 1800\\n     ```\\n   - Promote only if: no-brain fails or scores `<=85`, and Radar passes `>=92`. Otherwise drop it as saturated.\\n\\n**Avoid for now:** attribution-realign and review-file-count. Existing screens are mostly saturated/no-brain-too-easy, so they are unlikely to produce fair agent-lift proof.\"},\"019eb22a-8e82-7b11-a8f6-daf7ad5e5db4\":{\"completed\":\"No `Makefile` found; the actionable task surface is [mise.toml](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:6) plus the release/Radar docs. Also note the worktree is already dirty: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:488) has `44 -> 47` focused tests. I did not edit it.\\n\\n**Fastest Useful Sequence**\\n\\n1. **Current-code Radar/MCP contract smoke**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p go test ./internal/cli -run '^(TestRegression|TestInspectRegressions|TestMCP|TestWorkspaceRegressions)'\\n   ```\\n   Duration observed: ~2.6s for the retained 47-test regex; this broader regex should still be seconds.  \\n   Proves current branch code still passes the live MCP/Radar tests, not just the retained artifact.\\n\\n2. **Retained MCP/Radar tool evidence**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p mise run radar:evidence\\n   ```\\n   Duration observed: 0.17s, PASS.  \\n   Proves the committed deterministic MCP/Radar artifact is hash-valid and covers 47 required tests: location-only redaction, deletion opt-in, workspace Radar, strict MCP args, QMD MCP retrieval, and safe `tool_result` logging. This is citable tool-contract proof, not agent lift.\\n\\n3. **Thomas/Radar saturation screen**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p mise run radar:screen\\n   ```\\n   Duration observed: 0.25s.  \\n   Proves the Thomas question directly: whether Radar has real no-brain headroom or just saturation/audit gaps. Current result: 26 Radar comparisons, 0 proof-ready, 0 promotable; useful for deciding not to spend the next hour on saturated panels.\\n\\n4. **Retained replay-lab release evidence**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p mise run release:evidence\\n   ```\\n   Duration observed: 0.99s, PASS.  \\n   Proves retained release evidence is audit-clean for current manifest scopes: `history` and generic `mcp`. Current retained lane has 2 suites, 16 records, 4 MCP-verified records, 0 named/completed MCP tool records, so it supports generic MCP/history readiness but not Radar agent-lift.\\n\\n5. **Candidate task/panel preflight**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py check --tasks \\\\\\n     entireio-cli-radar-review-base-file-count.json \\\\\\n     entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions.json \\\\\\n     entireio-cli-manual-commit-attribution-base.json \\\\\\n     entireio-cli-transcript-reresolve.json\\n   ```\\n   Duration observed: ~20s, PASS.  \\n   Proves the committed Radar/MCP candidate tasks still fail as expected before agents run. This is high-signal and cheap before spending agent time.\\n\\n6. **Other retained claim gates**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p mise run distill:evidence\\n   /usr/bin/time -p mise run facts:evidence\\n   ```\\n   Durations observed: 0.16s and 0.12s, both PASS.  \\n   These are not Radar/MCP lift proof, but they keep release copy honest: distill has narrow scheduler-speed evidence; facts is explicit `no_release_claim`.\\n\\n7. **Semantic freshness gate, currently expected to fail**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p mise run semantic:evidence\\n   ```\\n   Duration observed: 1.08s, FAIL.  \\n   It reports `freshness=unsafe`, `head: stale`, `worktree: dirty-unindexed`. This is useful release-readiness signal, but do not burn time debugging Radar with this unless you are ready to refresh the local semantic index.\\n\\nI would not start with `mise run release:readiness` in a no-edit sidecar pass. It runs [check + all evidence gates](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:286), and `check` depends on lint tasks including `go mod tidy` via `lint:gomod`, which can modify `go.mod`/`go.sum`. For this next hour, the sequence above gives the best signal/time without touching files.\"},\"019eb218-4951-7fb1-9cac-97592b329318\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only scan only. I did not edit files, push, or run networked work.\\n\\n**Ranked Gaps**\\n\\n1. **High: `related_locations` can cross-link different invariants that share the same identifier.**  \\n   [regressionRelatedLocationMatch](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:1064) returns true when identifiers match, before comparing the normalized expected invariant. The new test covers different identifiers (`TranscriptPath` vs `ResolveMode`) in [regression_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression_test.go:369), but not same identifier with different RHS, e.g. `state.TranscriptPath = resolved` and `state.TranscriptPath = fallback`.  \\n   Suggested test: add a detector test where both missing deletions target `state.TranscriptPath` but have different RHS values, and assert `related_locations` only links same expected invariant. Implementation likely needs related matching keyed by normalized expected/target+rhs for deletions, not identifier alone.\\n\\n2. **High: retained Radar tool evidence can be stale and still pass audit.**  \\n   Current branch HEAD is `caf5d360…`, but the retained Radar tool manifest still records `source_head` as `209e5706…` in [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:80). The audit only verifies that `source_head` is 40 hex chars in [audit_radar_tool_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:129), and the test helper bakes in `\\\"a\\\" * 40` as acceptable in [run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:3464).  \\n   Suggested test: stale `source_head` should fail when the manifest is under the current repo, or add an explicit `--expected-source-head` gate and require release evidence to pass it.\\n\\n3. **Medium-high: `brain_review` / `brain_workspace_review` drop multi-locus context.**  \\n   Raw anomalies carry `Symbol` and `RelatedLocations` in [regression.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:48), but `reviewFinding` has no corresponding fields in [regression.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:1168), and [anomalyToReviewFinding](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:1206) discards them. Workspace review then maps anomalies through that lossy shape in [workspace.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:1059).  \\n   Suggested test: `brain_workspace_review` with `include_deletions:true, location_only:true` should preserve `symbol` and `related_locations`, or docs/tests should explicitly declare review tools non-authoritative for multi-locus Radar repair. Additive fields would not require a schema bump.\\n\\n4. **Medium: workspace scan helper is not self-protecting against unsafe repo pairing.**  \\n   `runWorkspaceRegressions` checks freshness before scanning in [workspace.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:978), but [scanWorkspaceRepoRegressions](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:934) independently resolves `LocalPathHint` and scans without re-checking the repo key pairing. Today callers are safe, but this is a brittle boundary and a TOCTOU opening.  \\n   Suggested test: fake runner returns matching repo key during freshness and mismatched key during scan, or call the helper directly with mismatched repo metadata and assert it refuses. Implementation: move pairing validation into the scan helper or pass a validated repo path/freshness object into it.\\n\\n5. **Medium-low: MCP debug log redacts args but not arbitrary tool names.**  \\n   [mcpDebugToolCall](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:114) strips control chars but logs the client-supplied tool name verbatim via [mcpDebugLogToolResult](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:145). Existing tests prove query args are not logged in [mcp_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:200), but not that an invalid tool name containing source/query text is suppressed.  \\n   Suggested test: send `tools/call` with an unknown name containing a canary string and assert the debug log records `unknown_tool` or nothing, not the raw name.\"},\"019eb218-2e2a-7a82-9d0c-49f4e4597681\":{\"completed\":\"**Audit Result**\\nRetained distill-performance evidence is already healthy for its narrow claim. I ran:\\n\\n```sh\\nmise run distill:evidence\\ngo test ./internal/cli -run 'TestRunDistillForBrainParallelExtractionMatchesSerial|TestExecOllamaDistillAgent|TestDistillDryRun|TestRunDistillForBrainReportsDistillEvidence'\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py DistillPerfAuditScriptTests\\n```\\n\\nAll passed. `mise run distill:evidence` reports release evidence true for current-repo command-agent scheduler proof, `159` chunks, and `1.996x` observed speedup.\\n\\n**What’s Done**\\n- Dry-run is implemented in [internal/cli/distill_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:656) via `buildDistillDryRunReport`, with CLI handling at [internal/cli/distill_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:264).\\n- Timing JSON is implemented in [internal/cli/facts.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts.go:42) and populated in [internal/cli/distill_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:623).\\n- `--jobs` extraction is parallelized but committed deterministically through ordered result consumption in [internal/cli/distill_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:934) and deterministic fact writes in [internal/cli/facts.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts.go:243).\\n- Ollama loopback runner is implemented in [internal/cli/distill_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1361), with proxy bypass, redirect checks, and loopback-only dialing.\\n\\n**Remaining Gaps**\\n- No production dry-run or `--jobs` determinism gap found.\\n- Current retained evidence in [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:1) proves only “current-repo local command-agent distill extraction scheduling speedup,” not real Ollama latency or a large frontend repo.\\n- Smallest code/test gap: Ollama is well tested at the runner level, but not through the full `entire brain distill --agent ollama --model ... --json` command path. Also `injectAgentModel` lacks an explicit Ollama assertion.\\n\\n**Lowest-Risk Next Patch After Radar/MCP**\\nMake it test-only unless a test exposes a bug:\\n\\n1. Add an Ollama case to `TestInjectAgentModel` in [internal/cli/distill_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_test.go:305).\\n2. Add `TestDistillCommandOllamaLoopbackProducesTimedSummary` in [internal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go:1594):\\n   - create a temp brain with `writeDistillFixtureAt`\\n   - serve `/api/generate` with `httptest`\\n   - set `ENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL`\\n   - run `distill --agent ollama --model llama3.2 --json --force --jobs 2`\\n   - assert request model/system/prompt, non-streaming, no PATH `ollama`, and JSON summary has `agent`, `model`, `jobs`, `effective_extraction_jobs`, call counts, and timing fields.\\n\\nRun after patch:\\n\\n```sh\\ngo test ./internal/cli -run 'TestDistillCommandOllamaLoopbackProducesTimedSummary|TestInjectAgentModel|TestExecOllamaDistillAgent'\\ngo test ./internal/cli\\nmise run distill:evidence\\n```\\n\\nWorktree note: `docs/release_readiness_audit.md` is currently modified with an unrelated MCP/Radar test-count change (`44` to `47`); I did not edit or revert it.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
