{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T16:26:15.722Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_A5tCmD8mK3L1sKMCfnUimJd0","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb1c9-da6e-7553-a01e-d6837efa84a3\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only sidecar audit complete on `codex/release-readiness-hardening` at `4aad581`. No edits, no PR/push/branch changes.\\n\\n**Top Gaps**\\n\\n1. [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:81](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:81) still says `source_head = caf5d36`, but current HEAD is `4aad581`, and `9271635` changed Radar proof gates, `regression.go`, `regression_test.go`, and the retained artifact. The artifact includes `TestRegressionAssignmentDeletionRelatedLocationsDistinguishSameIdentifierDifferentRHS`, which was added after `caf5d36`. [audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:130](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:130) only checks that `source_head` is shaped like a SHA.  \\nPatch recommendation: regenerate `go-test-internal-cli-radar.jsonl` from a clean committed head, update manifest hash/source_head/report, and make the audit fail if `source_head != git rev-parse HEAD` unless an explicit `--allow-stale-source-head` is passed. Add a `run_test.py` test that a stale `source_head` fails.\\n\\n2. [mise.toml:99](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:99) audits the retained Radar artifact but does not rerun the Go command, and [mise.toml:121](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:121) only regenerates audit reports, not the artifact or manifest. This lets stale deterministic evidence keep passing.  \\nPatch recommendation: add a `radar:evidence:record` or make `radar:evidence:update` run the manifest command, rewrite the JSONL artifact, recompute sha256, set `source_head`, then run the auditor.\\n\\n3. [benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:22](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:22) retains only Go/MCP tool tests. The false-proof gates live in Python tests around [benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2362](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2362), [run_test.py:2401](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2401), and [run_test.py:2440](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2440), but they are not retained in deterministic evidence.  \\nPatch recommendation: add a second retained artifact for focused Python proof-integrity tests, including same-call args+success for single/workspace Radar, unsafe server args, deletion policy, named-tool backing, and summary mismatch tests.\\n\\n4. [internal/cli/mcp_test.go:200](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:200) tests `brain_regressions` debug-log error redaction, and [mcp_test.go:223](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:223) tests successful `brain_workspace_regressions`. There is still no success debug-log/redaction test for `brain_review` or `brain_workspace_review`, even though [docs/diffless_review_seam.md:61](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/diffless_review_seam.md:61) discusses those tools as covered local contract surfaces.  \\nPatch recommendation: add a table-driven `TestMCPDebugLogReviewToolsRedactAndLogSuccess` for `brain_review` and `brain_workspace_review`, asserting `tool_args`, `tool_result: ... ok`, and no query/expected/current leakage. Add it to the Radar tool evidence required list.\\n\\n5. [benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:296](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:296) gives `mcp_radar_answer_assisted` an empty required arg set, so a successful `brain_regressions` call with `location_only:true` can satisfy answer-assisted named-tool completion.  \\nPatch recommendation: add a forbidden-args check or exact-mode check. For answer-assisted, reject `location_only:true`; add a test with `BENCH_REGRESSION_RADAR=1` plus a location-only server log and assert it is not completed answer-assisted proof.\\n\\n6. Workspace repo pairing validation is now good in the scanner path: [workspace.go:978](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:978) blocks `PairingUnsafe`, with tests for remote mismatch, sessions-only mismatch, and unverifiable local fallback at [workspace_test.go:680](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace_test.go:680), [workspace_test.go:754](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace_test.go:754), and [workspace_test.go:809](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace_test.go:809). Remaining proof gap: MCP evidence does not bind the workspace argument. [mcp.go:132](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:132) and [run.py:2410](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2410) preserve only boolean args, so a successful call to the wrong workspace can still look proof-valid.  \\nPatch recommendation: safe-log `workspace` as a validated name or hash, store expected workspace in provenance, require it in `audit_codex.py`, and add wrong-workspace tests.\\n\\nBottom line: deterministic evidence is directionally strong for the local tool contract, but it is not yet release-tight because it is stale/unbound to the current clean tree and omits the Python proof-integrity tests. Agent-lift evidence is correctly not claimed; the docs are appropriately cautious there.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
