{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T16:39:25.364Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Estimated time left depends on which finish line:\n\n- **Scoped PR-ready release-readiness branch:** about **30-60 min** for final audit notes/review prep. `mise run release:readiness` is green, working tree is clean, no PR/push happened.\n- **“Everything Thomas could possibly want” with real positive claims:** more like **1-2+ days**, mostly because Radar agent-lift and facts-vs-raw proof require slow benchmark evidence, not just code.\n\nWhat just improved:\n- Radar/MCP evidence is now **49 required tests**, not 48.\n- Added MCP review debug-log redaction coverage for `brain_review` and `brain_workspace_review`.\n- Hardened retained Radar evidence so stale source/test drift fails.\n- Refreshed semantic index and full release gate passed.\n\nSubagents helped find the gaps, but the bottleneck now is serial proof runs: benchmarks, evidence regeneration, race tests, and semantic refresh. More agents can audit in parallel, but they can’t make one benchmark suite finish instantly.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
