spect every top anomaly that shares the top anomaly's repo/file/kind before editing; when the top results list multiple line numbers in the same file, open each listed line and fix the shared invariant at all affected sites. Work out what the code should be by reading the surrounding code, and apply the fix yourself. Then run exactly one relevant test and FINISH. If it returns no anomalies, stop immediately and report `WORKSPACE_RADAR_NO_FINDINGS`. Do NOT call any other MCP tool, do NOT re-call, and keep `rg`/`grep`/`find` to at most 3 targeted in-file searches. Useful query terms: {queries}. Do not run the `entire brain` CLI or read `.benchmark/brain-history-excerpt.md`. If no Entire Brain MCP tools are visible, stop immediately and report `MCP_TOOLS_MISSING`.\"\"\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2158:        'mcp_servers.entire_brain.enabled_tools=[\"brain_stale\",\"brain_brief\",\"brain_query\",\"brain_search\",\"brain_vsearch\",\"brain_get\",\"brain_multi_get\",\"brain_context\",\"brain_impact\",\"brain_changes\",\"brain_regressions\",\"brain_review\",\"brain_workspace_regressions\",\"brain_workspace_review\"]',\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2216:            \"workspace-write\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:3390:            if condition == \"mcp_workspace_radar\":\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:3391:                return \"mcp_workspace_radar_location_only\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/full.json:21:  \"workspace_tasks\": [\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/full.json:25:      \"note\": \"Cross-repo workspace scenario per agent_benchmark_plan.md (\\\"Cross-repo workspace tasks\\\"): break a plugin dispatch / env assumption where the fix could plausibly live in entire-brain OR ../cli, and measure whether the multi-brain workspace localizes it. NOT yet wired into the panel runner — a runnable workspace task needs the workspace harness (two pinned member repos + a hidden cross-repo regression). Tracked here so the panel's multi-repo coverage gap is explicit, not 