{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T16:45:43.189Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"thread_goal_updated","threadId":"019eacc8-4c81-7c91-b807-b3c82bbba45d","turnId":"ab375a45-1ce3-4c4b-b407-cbc5d45b73d9","goal":{"threadId":"019eacc8-4c81-7c91-b807-b3c82bbba45d","objective":"now do it ; audit fully end to end; and fix ALL LOSE ends of the brain i know htsi might takes days; don't sotp until brain fully ifxed losed ends and fulyl aduit that that is the case ; use subagents etc; and make sure u finish thomas needs to th e mmaxium extent psosbiel; and do the full aduit ccle on it too end to end ; REQUIREMNTS; this is probraly should be read at around 256M tokens of usage; so yeha a lot of time; oh also IDC abt credits and cost so use fully infien sub agent tasks worflwos etc etc; finsih goal fully; should have abt 260k+ new lines of code etc; filling evyerhitng which is half made etc etc; at the end entire brain shoudl ebcoem full prodcution level relase with eveyrhting thomas wants , my token suage , my liens of code vaildaited end to end etc etc; spend all u can and go fast etc too","status":"active","tokensUsed":21194644,"timeUsedSeconds":78991,"createdAt":1781030922,"updatedAt":1781109943}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T16:45:43.246Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_8sT8L5JvUy9pZ6V6VLMWal7l","output":"{\"status\":{\"completed\":\"Gate baseline: `mise run release:readiness` passes. The remaining blockers are for broader Thomas-release acceptance claims, not the narrow local gate. I made no edits.\\n\\n1. **Radar/MCP agent-lift proof is still absent**\\n   - Proved by: `mise run radar:agent-evidence` fails with “Radar evidence has no proof-ready comparison.”\\n   - Corroborated by: `mise run radar:screen` reports 27 Radar comparisons, 0 proof-ready, 0 promotable.\\n   - Docs already admit it: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:540), [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:546).\\n   - Current proof is only tool-contract: [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:24).\\n   - Smallest close: run one non-saturated Radar/workspace task with 4 reps per side, retained named-tool MCP logs, and proof-ready outcome labels; then make `radar:agent-evidence` pass.\\n\\n2. **MCP release evidence still allows count-only proof, not named-tool proof**\\n   - Proved by: `mise run release:evidence` passes while retained audit reports `mcp_named_tool_verified_records: 0`.\\n   - Evidence gate minimum permits that: [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json:6), [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json:20).\\n   - Audit totals confirm it: [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/codex-audit-report.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/codex-audit-report.json:796), [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/codex-audit-report.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/codex-audit-report.json:832).\\n   - Docs call this out as not citable for named-tool or efficiency claims: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:477).\\n   - Smallest close: rerun the MCP proof with retained `tool:` plus `tool_result:` debug logs, require named-tool proof for `mcp`, and only claim efficiency after time/tokens are non-regressed.\\n\\n3. **Distill Ollama path is tested, but retained performance evidence is command-agent only**\\n   - Proved by: `go test ./internal/cli -run 'Test.*(Ollama|Distill|DryRun|Dry)' -count=1` passes, but `mise run distill:evidence` cites only local command-agent artifacts.\\n   - Manifest scope and commands show `--agent command`: [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:3), [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:19).\\n   - Limitations exclude hosted-model latency and broader claims: [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:77).\\n   - Docs list target-repo dry-run/timed artifacts as pending: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:585).\\n   - Smallest close: retain Ollama loopback dry-run plus serial/parallel timed artifacts for the Thomas target repo, or explicitly keep the release claim to current-repo command-agent scheduling only.\\n\\n4. **Facts-vs-raw positive claim is blocked, and the validator still has an aggregate loophole**\\n   - Proved by: `mise run facts:evidence` passes only because policy is `no_release_claim`.\\n   - Retained report says claimable false: [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/facts-eval-audit-report.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/facts-eval-audit-report.json:4).\\n   - Manifest explicitly says no facts-vs-raw claim is retained: [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/manifest.json:3), [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/manifest.json:9).\\n   - Loophole: [benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py:234) checks only non-empty summaries, while [audit_facts_eval.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py:264) and [audit_facts_eval.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py:329) trust comparison `n`, winner, significance, and claimability.\\n   - Smallest close: patch the audit to recompute paired IDs and metric `n` from retained summaries before accepting any positive facts-vs-raw claim; then add one regression fixture for forged aggregate `n`.\\n\\n5. **Status docs are honest, but acceptance scope needs to stay narrow**\\n   - Proved by docs: shipped claims are local/tool-contract/no-claim scoped in [docs/release_press_release.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:70), while pending proof is listed at [docs/release_press_release.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:83).\\n   - Release audit similarly narrows claim scopes: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:526).\\n   - Smallest close: either keep Thomas acceptance explicitly scoped to these narrow claims, or collect the three missing evidence packets above before making broader claims.\\n\\nMinimal patch/evidence plan: first make Radar/MCP named-tool proof citable, second retain Ollama distill evidence, third harden facts-vs-raw recomputation before any positive claim.\"}}"}}
