{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T16:46:20.265Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_TAFgeyOfNtswV3otntsBuOF3","output":"{\"status\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only scan only. I did not edit files, push, or run networked work.\\n\\n**Ranked Gaps**\\n\\n1. **High: `related_locations` can cross-link different invariants that share the same identifier.**  \\n   [regressionRelatedLocationMatch](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:1064) returns true when identifiers match, before comparing the normalized expected invariant. The new test covers different identifiers (`TranscriptPath` vs `ResolveMode`) in [regression_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression_test.go:369), but not same identifier with different RHS, e.g. `state.TranscriptPath = resolved` and `state.TranscriptPath = fallback`.  \\n   Suggested test: add a detector test where both missing deletions target `state.TranscriptPath` but have different RHS values, and assert `related_locations` only links same expected invariant. Implementation likely needs related matching keyed by normalized expected/target+rhs for deletions, not identifier alone.\\n\\n2. **High: retained Radar tool evidence can be stale and still pass audit.**  \\n   Current branch HEAD is `caf5d360…`, but the retained Radar tool manifest still records `source_head` as `209e5706…` in [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:80). The audit only verifies that `source_head` is 40 hex chars in [audit_radar_tool_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:129), and the test helper bakes in `\\\"a\\\" * 40` as acceptable in [run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:3464).  \\n   Suggested test: stale `source_head` should fail when the manifest is under the current repo, or add an explicit `--expected-source-head` gate and require release evidence to pass it.\\n\\n3. **Medium-high: `brain_review` / `brain_workspace_review` drop multi-locus context.**  \\n   Raw anomalies carry `Symbol` and `RelatedLocations` in [regression.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:48), but `reviewFinding` has no corresponding fields in [regression.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:1168), and [anomalyToReviewFinding](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/regression.go:1206) discards them. Workspace review then maps anomalies through that lossy shape in [workspace.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:1059).  \\n   Suggested test: `brain_workspace_review` with `include_deletions:true, location_only:true` should preserve `symbol` and `related_locations`, or docs/tests should explicitly declare review tools non-authoritative for multi-locus Radar repair. Additive fields would not require a schema bump.\\n\\n4. **Medium: workspace scan helper is not self-protecting against unsafe repo pairing.**  \\n   `runWorkspaceRegressions` checks freshness before scanning in [workspace.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:978), but [scanWorkspaceRepoRegressions](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:934) independently resolves `LocalPathHint` and scans without re-checking the repo key pairing. Today callers are safe, but this is a brittle boundary and a TOCTOU opening.  \\n   Suggested test: fake runner returns matching repo key during freshness and mismatched key during scan, or call the helper directly with mismatched repo metadata and assert it refuses. Implementation: move pairing validation into the scan helper or pass a validated repo path/freshness object into it.\\n\\n5. **Medium-low: MCP debug log redacts args but not arbitrary tool names.**  \\n   [mcpDebugToolCall](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:114) strips control chars but logs the client-supplied tool name verbatim via [mcpDebugLogToolResult](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:145). Existing tests prove query args are not logged in [mcp_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:200), but not that an invalid tool name containing source/query text is suppressed.  \\n   Suggested test: send `tools/call` with an unknown name containing a canary string and assert the debug log records `unknown_tool` or nothing, not the raw name.\"}}"}}
