{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T16:58:09.379Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_iMxuWs128vKBoDUuMIgofLqb","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb15c-ebdd-7010-8d01-d3308a5d263e\":{\"completed\":\"Implemented the minimal facts-vs-raw hardening patch. No PR/push, no staging, and I left unrelated dirty files untouched.\\n\\nChanged paths:\\n- [audit_facts_eval.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py:197)\\n- [run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2651)\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n- The audit now indexes retained summary results by task ID, rejects empty/duplicate IDs, recomputes missing A/B IDs, and verifies top-level comparison `n` from retained rows.\\n- It recomputes per-metric `n` from retained summaries before accepting a positive claim: all paired rows for `precision`, `useful_per_1k`, `tokens`, `latency_ms`; labeled paired rows for `recall`.\\n- `facts_vs_raw_claim` now requires the claimed metric’s retained `n` to match the comparison artifact before it can become claimable: [audit_facts_eval.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py:460).\\n\\nExact tests added:\\n- Happy-path fixture now has 12 retained rows matching `n: 12`: [run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2653)\\n- Forged aggregate `n=999` is rejected: [run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2724)\\n- Hidden missing paired ID is rejected even when comparison claims full pairing: [run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2741)\\n\\nChecks run:\\n- `python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py FactsEvalAuditScriptTests` - 13 tests OK\\n- `mise run facts:evidence` - PASS\\n- `git diff --check -- benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py` - PASS\\n\\nI did not run the full benchmark test suite; this was intentionally kept to the facts-eval audit/test surface.\"},\"019eb1c9-d797-73e1-a3cb-cd83ff65795d\":{\"completed\":\"Yes. Workspace Radar proof should bind the exact `workspace` argument. The workspace name selects the corpus, so `brain_workspace_regressions(location_only=true)` is not enough proof unless the successful server-side call used the same workspace the harness created and recorded.\\n\\nI saw a concurrent uncommitted patch already moving this in the right direction. I did not edit files.\\n\\n**Current Good Shape**\\n- MCP debug logging now records only safe booleans plus validated workspace for workspace tools: [internal/cli/mcp.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:132), [internal/cli/mcp.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:138).\\n- Workspace names are already constrained to safe identifiers, no paths: [internal/cli/workspace.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:685).\\n- Harness provenance now has `run_config.workspace_name`: [benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:725).\\n- Harness-side MCP audit now requires workspace in the tool details: [benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:1225).\\n- Independent audit can sanitize safe `workspace` strings and require them in server args: [benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:66), [benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:353).\\n\\n**Remaining Gaps**\\n- Test fixtures still omit workspace from synthetic workspace Radar records/logs: [benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:1581), [benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2533).\\n- The release-counting test still expects proof to pass with only `{\\\"location_only\\\": true}` in the server log, which is now correctly too weak: [benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2548).\\n- Add one explicit negative test for mismatched workspace: provenance says `release-radar`, activity/server log says another valid workspace, audit must flag `B:mcp_workspace_radar_missing_workspace` and `B:mcp_workspace_radar_server_missing_workspace`.\\n\\n**Smallest Safe Patch**\\n1. Update `_workspace_mcp_release_record` to set `provenance.run_config.workspace_name = \\\"release-radar\\\"` and include `workspace: \\\"release-radar\\\"` in both `agent_info.activity.mcp_tool_details` and `mcp_condition_audit.mcp_tool_details`.\\n2. Update workspace Radar server-log fixtures to write:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\\"location_only\\\":true,\\\"workspace\\\":\\\"release-radar\\\"}\\n   ```\\n   plus `include_deletions:true` where the synthetic task policy requires it.\\n3. Keep `query`, source paths, repo paths, and result snippets out of logs. Only validated workspace strings should be allowed; invalid workspace should stay unsafe/redacted by key/type only.\\n\\n**Checks Run**\\n- Passed: targeted Go MCP logging tests.\\n- Passed: `python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py -k mcp_condition_audit`.\\n- Failed as expected: `CodexAuditScriptTests.test_audit_codex_counts_workspace_radar_delivery_scope`, because the old fixture still omits workspace and now gets `hard_flags`.\"},\"019eb218-2e2a-7a82-9d0c-49f4e4597681\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only audit done. I did not edit, push, or revert anything.\\n\\n**Findings**\\n1. [docs/release_press_release.md:43](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:43) says “focused history and MCP/Radar proofs.” That can read like retained Radar agent-lift proof exists. Evidence says Radar is tool-contract only.\\nSuggested:\\n`More replay-lab evidence beyond the first retained focused history proof, the retained generic MCP-history replay proof, and the deterministic MCP/Radar tool-contract proof...`\\n\\n2. [docs/release_press_release.md:36](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:36) says large-repo distill needs “a timed run.” The retained validator requires paired serial/parallel runs.\\nSuggested:\\n`Distill performance on a large session repo, using distill --dry-run --json plus paired timed --jobs 1 and --jobs N runs with cache/timing fields.`\\n\\n3. [docs/release_readiness_audit.md:488](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:488) says “48 focused internal/cli tests,” but retained Radar-tool evidence requires/passes 49.\\nSuggested:\\n`artifact over 49 focused internal/cli tests. It proves local QMD-inspired MCP tool...`\\n\\n4. [docs/release_press_release.md:73](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:73) says semantic audit coverage is “Proven locally.” That was true for a clean refreshed checkout, but current worktree is dirty and `mise run semantic:evidence` now fails with `freshness=degraded`, `worktree=dirty-unindexed`.\\nSuggested:\\n`Previously proven locally on a clean refreshed checkout: semantic audit coverage; rerun semantic:evidence on the final clean release head before citing.`\\n\\n5. [docs/release_readiness_audit.md:204](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:204) through [docs/release_readiness_audit.md:216](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:216) records historical semantic counts. Current direct audit reports `142 files`, `2,552 symbols`, `19,128 relations`, but fails release freshness due dirty worktree.\\nSuggested: prefix that paragraph with `Historical clean semantic evidence:` and add `The final release head must rerun mise run semantic:evidence on a clean worktree before this is current release evidence.`\\n\\n6. [docs/release_press_release.md:77](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:77) cites history proof improvement but does not say it was not an efficiency proof. The retained summary shows higher time/tokens for `full_brain`.\\nSuggested:\\n`one retained replay-lab history proof where full_brain improved task score/pass-rate over no_brain, without proving efficiency gains`\\n\\n**Evidence Check**\\nPassed:\\n```sh\\nmise run release:evidence\\nmise run radar:evidence\\nmise run facts:evidence\\nmise run distill:evidence\\n```\\n\\nCurrently failing because of dirty worktree:\\n```sh\\nmise run semantic:evidence\\n```\\n\\nCurrent modified non-doc files:\\n`benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py`, `audit_facts_eval.py`, `run.py`, `run_test.py`, `internal/cli/mcp.go`, `internal/cli/mcp_test.go`.\"},\"019eb218-4951-7fb1-9cac-97592b329318\":{\"completed\":\"**Findings**\\n\\n1. **P1: MCP QMD evidence does not actually prove `brain_query` facts retrieval, and `brain_vsearch` can be empty unnoticed.**  \\n   `brain_query`/`brain_vsearch` are advertised as QMD retrieval tools in [internal/cli/mcp.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:249), but `TestMCPQMDRetrievalToolsUseLocalFacts` only calls `brain_search`, `brain_vsearch`, `brain_get`, and `brain_multi_get`, not `brain_query` ([internal/cli/mcp_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:742)). Its aggregate substring assertion ([internal/cli/mcp_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:754)) would still pass if `brain_vsearch` returned no results.  \\n   Suggested test: extend this test to call `brain_query` with `branch`, parse each MCP `content[0].text` JSON separately, and assert `brain_search`, `brain_vsearch`, and `brain_query` each return the expected branch-scoped fact ID.\\n\\n2. **P1/P2: `mcp_semantic` benchmark policy still overclaims `brain_query` as semantic-graph context.**  \\n   The runner tells `mcp_semantic` agents to use `brain_query` for “focused semantic context” ([benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2087)), while `brain_query` is now unified facts/history/docs retrieval ([internal/cli/mcp.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:249)); semantic graph search is `brain_code` ([internal/cli/mcp.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:289)). The README also says `mcp_semantic` is “semantic tools only” ([benchmarks/agent-brain/README.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/README.md:119)).  \\n   Suggested test: add/adjust a `run_test.py` prompt assertion so `mcp_semantic` either uses `brain_code`/`brain_context`/`brain_impact`/`brain_changes`, or the docs/policy relabel it as semantic plus unified retrieval.\\n\\n3. **P2: CLI `--branch` behavior is exposed but not behaviorally pinned across QMD verbs.**  \\n   The flags exist for `search`/`vsearch`/`query` ([internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:46)), `get` ([internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:103)), and `multi-get` ([internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:125)). Current tests cover aliases/help, but the main alias test relies on the fake current branch instead of passing `--branch` ([internal/cli/retrieve_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_test.go:136)).  \\n   Suggested test: seed `main` and `feature` facts, then assert `search`, `query`, `vsearch`, `get`, and `multi-get --branch feature` return only feature facts and wrong-branch `get` reports missing.\\n\\n4. **P2/P3: `get`/`multi-get` JSON omits resolved branch, unlike search/query/vsearch.**  \\n   Retrieval JSON includes `branch` ([internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:69)), but `runGet` emits only `results` and `missing` ([internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:161)). This makes branch-scoped fetches harder to audit from MCP text results.  \\n   Suggested test/implementation: either add `branch` to `runGet` JSON and test it, or explicitly document/test that `get`/`multi-get` intentionally omit branch.\\n\\n5. **P3: release audit doc has stale evidence count.**  \\n   The doc says the Radar tool artifact covers 48 focused tests ([docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:486)), but the current auditor and manifest list 49 required tests ([benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_tool_evidence.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:32), [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:30)).  \\n   Suggested fix: update the doc or avoid hard-coding the count in release copy.\\n\\nVerification run: `go test ./internal/cli -run 'TestQMD|TestMCPQMD|TestMCPBrainQueryToolUsesLocalSemanticJSON|TestMCPBrainBriefAndQueryToolsUseIndexedHistory'` passed. No network used and I did not edit files. Note: `git status` currently shows modified files from other work; I left them untouched.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
