{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:01:16.994Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Current status: much better than when you asked.\n\nI used the sidecars, and they did speed this up by finding/patching parallel audit gaps while I handled integration. The hard serial bottleneck is still unavoidable: evidence recording needs a clean source commit, and `mise run release:readiness` has to run end-to-end.\n\nDone just now:\n- Strengthened MCP/Radar workspace proof so it binds the exact `workspace` arg.\n- Hardened facts-vs-raw audit against forged aggregate `n`.\n- Added retained fake-loopback Ollama contract evidence: 9/9 required local/no-egress tests.\n- Strengthened MCP QMD proof so `brain_query`, `brain_search`, `brain_vsearch`, `brain_get`, and `brain_multi_get` are each verified separately.\n- Refreshed retained Radar/distill evidence.\n- Ran `mise run release:readiness` at final HEAD `1fa11e4`: passed.\n- Worktree is clean.\n- Branch is `codex/release-readiness-hardening`.\n- No PR, no push.\n\nProgress estimate:\n- Local release-readiness gate: green, basically 100% for the current local proof suite.\n- Thomas full production asks: more like 70-80% locally, because real large-repo distill proof, facts-vs-raw positive evidence, and Radar agent-lift proof still require retained real benchmark data.\n- Time left for a strong “best PR” package: probably 1 focused pass to audit remaining docs/claims and maybe run/preserve one Radar agent-lift attempt. True production proof on huge repos could still be hours to days depending the dataset.\n\nToken usage now: about 21.44M tokens.\n\n::git-commit{cwd=\"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain\"}","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
