{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:05:17.915Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_elt7NwrWMXuEmERyYEUFWa8b","output":"{\"status\":{\"completed\":\"Yes. Workspace Radar proof should bind the exact `workspace` argument. The workspace name selects the corpus, so `brain_workspace_regressions(location_only=true)` is not enough proof unless the successful server-side call used the same workspace the harness created and recorded.\\n\\nI saw a concurrent uncommitted patch already moving this in the right direction. I did not edit files.\\n\\n**Current Good Shape**\\n- MCP debug logging now records only safe booleans plus validated workspace for workspace tools: [internal/cli/mcp.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:132), [internal/cli/mcp.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:138).\\n- Workspace names are already constrained to safe identifiers, no paths: [internal/cli/workspace.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/workspace.go:685).\\n- Harness provenance now has `run_config.workspace_name`: [benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:725).\\n- Harness-side MCP audit now requires workspace in the tool details: [benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:1225).\\n- Independent audit can sanitize safe `workspace` strings and require them in server args: [benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:66), [benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:353).\\n\\n**Remaining Gaps**\\n- Test fixtures still omit workspace from synthetic workspace Radar records/logs: [benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:1581), [benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2533).\\n- The release-counting test still expects proof to pass with only `{\\\"location_only\\\": true}` in the server log, which is now correctly too weak: [benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2548).\\n- Add one explicit negative test for mismatched workspace: provenance says `release-radar`, activity/server log says another valid workspace, audit must flag `B:mcp_workspace_radar_missing_workspace` and `B:mcp_workspace_radar_server_missing_workspace`.\\n\\n**Smallest Safe Patch**\\n1. Update `_workspace_mcp_release_record` to set `provenance.run_config.workspace_name = \\\"release-radar\\\"` and include `workspace: \\\"release-radar\\\"` in both `agent_info.activity.mcp_tool_details` and `mcp_condition_audit.mcp_tool_details`.\\n2. Update workspace Radar server-log fixtures to write:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\\"location_only\\\":true,\\\"workspace\\\":\\\"release-radar\\\"}\\n   ```\\n   plus `include_deletions:true` where the synthetic task policy requires it.\\n3. Keep `query`, source paths, repo paths, and result snippets out of logs. Only validated workspace strings should be allowed; invalid workspace should stay unsafe/redacted by key/type only.\\n\\n**Checks Run**\\n- Passed: targeted Go MCP logging tests.\\n- Passed: `python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py -k mcp_condition_audit`.\\n- Failed as expected: `CodexAuditScriptTests.test_audit_codex_counts_workspace_radar_delivery_scope`, because the old fixture still omits workspace and now gets `hard_flags`.\"}}"}}
