{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:05:28.919Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_zfvMHfzlOdgj6f3zw6XZ1nSg","output":"{\"status\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only audit done. I did not edit, push, or revert anything.\\n\\n**Findings**\\n1. [docs/release_press_release.md:43](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:43) says “focused history and MCP/Radar proofs.” That can read like retained Radar agent-lift proof exists. Evidence says Radar is tool-contract only.\\nSuggested:\\n`More replay-lab evidence beyond the first retained focused history proof, the retained generic MCP-history replay proof, and the deterministic MCP/Radar tool-contract proof...`\\n\\n2. [docs/release_press_release.md:36](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:36) says large-repo distill needs “a timed run.” The retained validator requires paired serial/parallel runs.\\nSuggested:\\n`Distill performance on a large session repo, using distill --dry-run --json plus paired timed --jobs 1 and --jobs N runs with cache/timing fields.`\\n\\n3. [docs/release_readiness_audit.md:488](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:488) says “48 focused internal/cli tests,” but retained Radar-tool evidence requires/passes 49.\\nSuggested:\\n`artifact over 49 focused internal/cli tests. It proves local QMD-inspired MCP tool...`\\n\\n4. [docs/release_press_release.md:73](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:73) says semantic audit coverage is “Proven locally.” That was true for a clean refreshed checkout, but current worktree is dirty and `mise run semantic:evidence` now fails with `freshness=degraded`, `worktree=dirty-unindexed`.\\nSuggested:\\n`Previously proven locally on a clean refreshed checkout: semantic audit coverage; rerun semantic:evidence on the final clean release head before citing.`\\n\\n5. [docs/release_readiness_audit.md:204](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:204) through [docs/release_readiness_audit.md:216](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:216) records historical semantic counts. Current direct audit reports `142 files`, `2,552 symbols`, `19,128 relations`, but fails release freshness due dirty worktree.\\nSuggested: prefix that paragraph with `Historical clean semantic evidence:` and add `The final release head must rerun mise run semantic:evidence on a clean worktree before this is current release evidence.`\\n\\n6. [docs/release_press_release.md:77](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:77) cites history proof improvement but does not say it was not an efficiency proof. The retained summary shows higher time/tokens for `full_brain`.\\nSuggested:\\n`one retained replay-lab history proof where full_brain improved task score/pass-rate over no_brain, without proving efficiency gains`\\n\\n**Evidence Check**\\nPassed:\\n```sh\\nmise run release:evidence\\nmise run radar:evidence\\nmise run facts:evidence\\nmise run distill:evidence\\n```\\n\\nCurrently failing because of dirty worktree:\\n```sh\\nmise run semantic:evidence\\n```\\n\\nCurrent modified non-doc files:\\n`benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py`, `audit_facts_eval.py`, `run.py`, `run_test.py`, `internal/cli/mcp.go`, `internal/cli/mcp_test.go`.\"}}"}}
