{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:08:42.437Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_SvYM8Ok88xmuGnvyQUvjoMPk","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb218-4951-7fb1-9cac-97592b329318\":{\"completed\":\"**P0/P1 Blockers**\\n\\nNone found in the current branch for the QMD/MCP surface. The earlier blockers look fixed: MCP now calls/asserts `brain_query` alongside `brain_search`, `brain_vsearch`, `brain_get`, and `brain_multi_get` in [internal/cli/mcp_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:742), and `mcp_semantic` no longer presents `brain_query` as semantic graph search in [benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2105).\\n\\n**P2 Gaps**\\n\\n1. CLI `--branch` override behavior is still mostly advertised, not behaviorally pinned.  \\n   Flags are wired for all verbs in [internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:46) and passed through at [internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:61), but CLI tests seed the fake current branch and do not pass `--branch` ([internal/cli/retrieve_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_test.go:147)). MCP branch behavior is better covered.\\n\\n2. `get`/`multi-get` JSON does not include resolved `branch`, unlike search/query/vsearch.  \\n   Retrieval JSON includes `branch` at [internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:69), but `runGet` emits only `results` and `missing` at [internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:161). This is not necessarily wrong, but it weakens auditability for branch-scoped fetches.\\n\\n3. `--limit` / `-n` precedence is only pinned on `search`.  \\n   The implementation is shared in [internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:29), so risk is low, but `TestQMDLimitAliasesAndPrecedence` only exercises `search` ([internal/cli/retrieve_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_test.go:219)). `query`/`vsearch` get lighter alias coverage.\\n\\n4. MCP schema test could assert the full required-field contract, not just branch/minItems.  \\n   Schemas correctly set required fields via [internal/cli/mcp.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:230), but the QMD schema test currently checks branch and `multi_get` `minItems` only ([internal/cli/mcp_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:116)).\\n\\n5. Release doc still says 48 focused tests while the retained Radar/QMD contract now has 49.  \\n   See [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:494) vs required test list starting at [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:30).\\n\\n**Recommended Fixes**\\n\\nAdd one CLI branch-override table test covering `search`, `query`, `vsearch`, `get`, and `multi-get` with a non-current branch and wrong-branch negative case. Decide whether `get`/`multi-get` JSON should include `branch`; either add it and test it, or document the omission. Expand limit precedence over `query` and `vsearch`, and strengthen MCP schema assertions for `required` and `limit.minimum`.\\n\\nVerification: focused Go QMD/MCP tests passed. The two benchmark runner-policy tests passed with corrected invocation. No network, no edits, no PR/push.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
