{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:14:28.380Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_b7pJNT60lUQdD1cP7HjHt8tM","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb218-2e2a-7a82-9d0c-49f4e4597681\":{\"completed\":\"No edits made. No P0 blockers found.\\n\\n**P1 Blockers**\\n1. Semantic “current checkout” claim is stale/false right now.\\n   `mise run semantic:evidence` failed with `freshness=unsafe`, `head: stale`, and `worktree: dirty-unindexed semantic index is based on committed HEAD`.\\n\\n   Affected:\\n   - [docs/release_press_release.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:52)\\n   - [docs/release_press_release.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:73)\\n   - [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:212)\\n\\n   Suggested replacement for press lines 51-54:\\n   ```md\\n   - Large-repo distill timing, paired facts evals, semantic usefulness, and broader\\n     multi-task replay evidence are still pending. Semantic audit coverage has\\n     historical local clean evidence after refresh, but the final release checkout\\n     must pass `mise run semantic:evidence` before citing current semantic health.\\n   ```\\n\\n   Suggested replacement for press line 73:\\n   ```md\\n   - Proven locally: historical semantic audit coverage after refresh on earlier\\n     clean checkpoints, pending a fresh `mise run semantic:evidence` pass on the\\n     final clean release checkout,\\n   ```\\n\\n2. “MCP/Radar proofs” reads like retained Radar agent-lift proof exists. It does not.\\n   The retained release manifest has only `history` + generic `mcp` proof scopes; Radar is separate tool-contract evidence only.\\n\\n   Affected:\\n   - [docs/release_press_release.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:43)\\n\\n   Suggested replacement:\\n   ```md\\n   - More replay-lab evidence beyond the first retained focused history proof and\\n     retained generic MCP-history proof, plus separate deterministic Radar\\n     tool-contract evidence; Radar agent-lift still needs repeated benchmark\\n     scenarios, stable verdicts, and committed release/Radar audit reports.\\n   ```\\n\\n**P2 Issues**\\n1. Stale Radar tool-test count: one paragraph says 48, but manifest/report/gate say 49.\\n   Affected: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:496)\\n\\n   Replace `48 focused` with `49 focused`.\\n\\n2. QMD wording drifts from the doc’s own policy. Line 335 says release claims should say “QMD-inspired aliases,” but later text says “QMD-style.”\\n   Affected:\\n   - [docs/release_press_release.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:81)\\n   - [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:312)\\n   - [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:11)\\n\\n   Suggested replacement: use `local QMD-inspired` instead of `QMD-style`.\\n\\n3. Distill proof wording under-specifies the retained evidence shape.\\n   Affected: [docs/release_press_release.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md:36)\\n\\n   Suggested replacement:\\n   ```md\\n   - Distill performance on a large session repo, using `distill --dry-run --json`\\n     plus paired timed `--jobs 1` and `--jobs N` JSON runs with matching\\n     cache/timing fields.\\n   ```\\n\\n4. README release-gate description is stale/incomplete versus the manifest.\\n   Affected: [benchmarks/agent-brain/README.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/README.md:273)\\n\\n   Suggested replacement:\\n   ```md\\n   That gate reads `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json`,\\n   audits only suite directories matching `release-candidate-*`, rejects\\n   `release-local-*`, and enforces the manifest thresholds: currently 2 suites,\\n   16 records, 2 proof-ready comparisons, 4 repetitions per side, panel\\n   provenance, zero hard flags, at least one proof-ready comparison per retained\\n   suite, and required proof scopes `history` and generic `mcp`.\\n   ```\\n\\n5. README quarantine sentence is stale now that retained release evidence exists.\\n   Affected: [benchmarks/agent-brain/README.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/README.md:290)\\n\\n   Suggested replacement:\\n   ```md\\n   Ignored `results/` panels remain quarantine/reference evidence unless copied or\\n   regenerated into the provenance-complete retained lane under\\n   `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release` and passing `mise run release:evidence`.\\n   ```\\n\\n6. One release-readiness sentence says only one focused history proof is retained, but generic MCP-history proof is now retained too.\\n   Affected: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:627)\\n\\n   Suggested replacement:\\n   ```md\\n   One focused history proof and one generic MCP-history proof are now retained;\\n   semantic/facts, Radar agent-lift, and broader multi-task replay evidence are\\n   still needed for broader claims.\\n   ```\\n\\nVerification run locally: `release:evidence`, `radar:evidence`, `distill:evidence`, and `facts:evidence` pass. `radar:screen` now reports 27 Radar comparisons, 0 proof-ready, 0 promotable; the requested docs do not embed the old 25 count.\"},\"019eb1c9-d797-73e1-a3cb-cd83ff65795d\":{\"completed\":\"No P0 found for the scoped retained gates. The workspace binding fix itself looks solid: server logging only admits validated `workspace` for workspace Radar/review tools, and the harness/audit now require `provenance.run_config.workspace_name` to match the server/activity args.\\n\\n**P1 Blockers**\\n\\n1. **No retained Radar agent-lift or workspace Radar proof yet.**  \\n   The retained release manifest only requires `history` and generic `mcp` proof scopes, not Radar: [manifest.json:20](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json:20). The release README also says recent Radar panels are saturated/noisy and not retained as release evidence: [README.md:59](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/README.md:59).  \\n   I also confirmed `audit_radar_evidence.py --fail-when-no-proof` fails with `Radar comparisons: 0`.  \\n   Smallest fix: keep release claims scoped to deterministic Radar/MCP tool-contract proof, or retain a fresh non-saturated Radar/workspace-Radar panel under `evidence/release` and add the Radar scope to `required_proof_scopes` plus `required_named_tool_proof_scopes`.\\n\\n2. **Retained MCP pass-rate evidence is not named-tool / `tool_result` backed.**  \\n   The retained audit passes with `MCP verified records: 4`, but named/completed server proof is zero: [codex-audit-report.md:6](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/codex-audit-report.md:6). The manifest explicitly permits that with `mcp_named_tool_verified_records: 0`: [manifest.json:10](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json:10), and no required named-tool scopes: [manifest.json:24](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/manifest.json:24).  \\n   Smallest fix: do not cite retained generic MCP as server-named/tool-result proof. If that claim is needed, rerun the MCP panel with current debug logging retained, then raise the manifest minimums and require named-tool proof for `mcp`.\\n\\n3. **Radar tool evidence drift gate is blind to QMD retrieval files and dirty local changes.**  \\n   The Radar tool manifest claims QMD retrieval coverage: [manifest.json:9](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:9), but the source-drift allowlist only watches regression/MCP/workspace files: [audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:23](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:23). It compares those watched files to `source_head`: [audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:139](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_radar_tool_evidence.py:139). Current dirty relevant files include `internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go` and `internal/cli/retrieve_test.go`, yet `mise run radar:evidence` still passes.  \\n   Smallest fix: add QMD retrieval implementation/tests to `RADAR_TOOL_SOURCE_PATHS` and fail on dirty watched paths before citing retained tool-contract evidence.\\n\\n**P2 Gaps**\\n\\n- Docs are stale on safe logging. [docs/diffless_review_seam.md:131](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/diffless_review_seam.md:131) still says only safe boolean args are recorded, but workspace Radar now also records validated `workspace`. Quick fix: document “safe booleans plus validated workspace only; never query/source/current.”\\n\\n- `audit_codex.py` treats `workspace` as a globally safe server string arg: [audit_codex.py:50](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py:50). Server-side emission is narrower, so this is not immediately unsafe, but the audit could be stricter. Quick fix: make safe string args tool-aware and flag `workspace` on non-workspace tools.\\n\\n- Release README could make the new binding rule explicit. It already says future Radar proof needs named `tool:` and `tool_result:` logs: [README.md:15](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/README.md:15). Quick fix: add that workspace Radar proof must bind server `tool_args.workspace` to `provenance.run_config.workspace_name`.\\n\\n**Verified**\\n\\n- `mise run release:evidence` passed.\\n- `mise run radar:evidence` passed.\\n- Focused MCP/Radar Go tests passed.\\n- Focused benchmark audit tests passed.\\n- `mise run radar:agent-evidence` failed as expected because no retained Radar proof-ready comparison exists.\\n\\nNo files edited, no network, no PR/push.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
