XACTLY ONCE with `workspace: \"{workspace}\"`, query terms `{queries}`, and {radar_arg_hint}.{radar_shape_note} It returns the suspected workspace repo plus `file` and `line` of the regression but NOT the fix. Treat any `symbol` and `related_locations` fields as location-only hints: inspect the enclosing symbol and every related same-file location before editing. Inspect every top anomaly that shares the top anomaly's repo/file/kind before editing; when the top results list multiple line numbers in the same file, open each listed line and fix the shared invariant at all affected sites. Work out what the code should be by reading the surrounding code, and apply the fix yourself. Then run exactly one relevant test and FINISH. If it returns no anomalies, stop immediately and report `WORKSPACE_RADAR_NO_FINDINGS`. Do NOT call any other MCP tool, do NOT re-call, and keep `rg`/`grep`/`find` to at most 3 targeted in-file searches. Useful query terms: {queries}. Do not run the `entire brain` CLI or read `.benchmark/brain-history-excerpt.md`. If no Entire Brain MCP tools are visible, stop immediately and report `MCP_TOOLS_MISSING`.\"\"\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2112:    elif condition == \"mcp_history\" and wants_radar_location_only(runner):\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2113:        # FAIR radar arm: brain_regressions(location_only) hands the suspected file:line but NOT the\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2115:        policy = f\"\"\"Use the Entire Brain MCP server before any shell search or file reads. If your client exposes a `WaitForMcpServers` tool, first wait for the `entire_brain` server. This task is a REGRESSION. Call `mcp__entire_brain__brain_regressions` / `brain_regressions` EXACTLY ONCE with {radar_arg_hint} and these failing terms: `{queries}`.{radar_shape_note} It returns the suspected `file` and `line` of the regression but NOT the fix. Treat any `symbol` and `related_locations` fields as location-only hints: inspect the enclosing symbol and every related same-file location before editing. Inspect every top anomaly that shares the top anomaly's file/kind before editing; when the top results list multiple line numbers in the same file, open each listed line and fix the shared invariant at all affected sites. Work out what the code should be by reading the surrounding code, and apply the fix yourself. Then run exactly one relevant test and FINISH. If it returns no anomalies, call `brain_brief` ONCE and fix the single most likely `likely_edit_files` file. Do NOT call any other MCP tool, do NOT re-call, and keep `rg`/`grep`/`find` to at most 3 targeted in-file searches. Useful query terms: {queries}. Do not run the `entire brain` CLI or read `.benchmark/brain-history-excerpt.md`. If no Entire Brain MCP tools are visible, stop immediately and report `MCP_TOOLS_MISSING`.\"\"\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2116:    elif condition == \"mcp_history\" and wants_regression_radar(runner):\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2117:        # ANSWER-ASSISTED radar arm (UPPER BOUND, not a fair detection measure): brain_regressions\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2120:        policy = f\"\"\"Use the Entire Brain MCP server before any shell search or file reads. If your client exposes a `WaitForMcpServers` tool, first wait for the `entire_brain` server. This task is a REGRESSION. Call `mcp__entire_brain__brain_regressions` / `brain_regressions` EXACTLY ONCE with these failing terms: `{queries}` and {\"`include_deletions: true`\" if task.get(\"radar_include_deletions\") else \"no extra deletion flag\"}.{radar_shape_note} It returns suspected regressions, each with a `file`, `line`, the `expected` value (what the code should be) and the `current` value. Open the top finding's `file` at its `line` and restore `expected` exactly in place of `current`. Then run exactly one relevant test and FINISH. If `brain_regressions` returns no anomalies, call `brain_brief` ONCE and fix the single most likely `likely_edit_files` file. Do NOT call any other MCP tool, do NOT re-call, and keep `rg`/`grep`/`find` to at most 2 targeted in-file searches. Useful query terms: {queries}. Do not run the `entire brain` CLI or read `.benchmark/brain-history-excerpt.md`. If no Entire Brain MCP tools are visible, stop immediately and report `MCP_TOOLS_MISSING`.\"\"\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:3451:            if condition == \"mcp_workspace_radar\":\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:3452:                return \"mcp_workspace_radar_location_only\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:3454:                return \"mcp_radar_location_only\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:3456:                return \"mcp_radar_answer_assisted\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions.json:2:  \"id\": \"entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions.json:13:  \"radar_include_deletions\": true,\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions.json:46:    \"release-radar-manual-attribution-deletions-canary-20260610T1040Z\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve-haiku-xhigh.json:2:  \"name\": \"release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve-haiku-xhigh\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve-haiku-xhigh.json:3:  \"description\": \"Focused MCP workspace-radar release-candidate panel for the deletion-shaped transcript re-resolution regression on a harder runner. Prior local screening showed no-brain headroom for claude:haiku:xhigh; the Radar arm remains location-only through mcp_workspace_radar and the task declares radar_include_deletions.\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve-haiku-xhigh.json:9:    \"mcp_workspace_radar\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve-haiku-xhigh.json:13:    \"entireio-cli-transcript-reresolve.json\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entireio-cli-radar-review-base-file-count.json:2:  \"id\": \"entireio-cli-radar-review-base-file-count\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entireio-cli-radar-review-base-file-count.json:22:    \"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nPath('cmd/entire/cli/review/scope_radar_hidden_test.go').write_text(r'''package review\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"context\\\"\\n\\t\\\"os/exec\\\"\\n\\t\\\"testing\\\"\\n)\\n\\nfunc TestComputeScopeStats_BaseOverrideFileCountUsesOverride(t *testing.T) {\\n\\tdir := t.TempDir()\\n\\tinitRepoOnMain(t, dir)\\n\\tcommitFile(t, dir, \\\"root.go\\\", \\\"package main\\\", \\\"init\\\")\\n\\n\\trun := func(args ...string) {\\n\\t\\tt.Helper()\\n\\t\\tcmd := exec.Command(\\\"git\\\", args...)\\n\\t\\tcmd.Dir = dir\\n\\t\\tif out, err := cmd.CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"git %v: %v\\\\n%s\\\", args, err, out)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\trun(\\\"checkout\\\", \\\"-b\\\", \\\"feat/parent\\\")\\n\\tcommitFile(t, dir, \\\"parent.go\\\", \\\"package main\\\", \\\"parent\\\")\\n\\trun(\\\"checkout\\\", \\\"-b\\\", \\\"feat/child\\\")\\n\\tcommitFile(t, dir, \\\"child.go\\\", \\\"package main\\\", \\\"child\\\")\\n\\trun(\\\"checkout\\\", \\\"main\\\")\\n\\tcommitFile(t, dir, \\\"main_only.go\\\", \\\"package main\\\", \\\"main only\\\")\\n\\trun(\\\"checkout\\\", \\\"feat/child\\\")\\n\\n\\tstats, err := ComputeScopeStats(context.Background(), openTestRepo(t, dir), \\\"feat/parent\\\")\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\tt.Fatal(err)\\n\\t}\\n\\tif stats.FilesChanged != 1 {\\n\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"FilesChanged = %d, want 1; explicit base must not use main...HEAD\\\", stats.FilesChanged)\\n\\t}\\n}\\n''')\\nPY\\nrc=0\\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/review -run '^TestComputeScopeStats_BaseOverrideFileCountUsesOverride$' -count=1 || rc=$?\\nrm -f cmd/entire/cli/review/scope_radar_hidden_test.go\\nexit $rc\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entireio-cli-radar-review-base-file-count.json:35:    \"release-radar-review-base-file-count-canary-20260610T0730Z\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution.json:2:  \"name\": \"release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution.json:3:  \"description\": \"Focused release-candidate Regression Radar panel for the manual-commit attribution-base regression. The location-only MCP radar may reveal the suspected manual_commit_hooks file/line, but not the missing realignment call or expected/current values.\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-mcp-manual-attribution.json:2:  \"name\": \"release-entire-cli-mcp-manual-attribution\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-mcp-manual-attribution.json:3:  \"description\": \"Focused release-candidate MCP-history panel for the manual-commit attribution-base regression. This is a harder non-radar MCP proof lane: the brain should supply the historical invariant and likely file, while the agent still has to repair the code without hidden validation or expected text.\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions.json:2:  \"name\": \"release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions.json:3:  \"description\": \"Focused release-candidate Regression Radar panel for the deletion-shaped manual-commit attribution-base regression. The location-only MCP radar may reveal the suspected manual_commit_hooks file/line, including deleted realignment calls, but not the expected/current values.\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions.json:16:    \"entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions.json\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve.json:2:  \"name\": \"release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve.json:3:  \"description\": \"Focused MCP workspace-radar calibration panel for a deletion-shaped transcript re-resolution regression. The task declares radar_include_deletions and the mcp_workspace_radar condition calls brain_workspace_regressions with location_only so the tool localizes the repo/file/line while withholding expected/current fix text.\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve.json:9:    \"mcp_workspace_radar\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-workspace-radar-mcp-transcript-reresolve.json:13:    \"entireio-cli-transcript-reresolve.json\"\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/swe-style-entire-cli-transcript-reresolve.json:2:  \"id\": \"swe-style-entire-cli-transcript-reresolve\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/swe-style-entire-cli-transcript-reresolve.json:6:  \"suite_tags\": [\"swe-style\", \"entire-cli\", \"transcript\"],\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/swe-style-entire-cli-transcript-reresolve.json:8:  \"prompt\": \"Issue: after an agent moves its transcript from the originally stored path, the resolver finds the relocated file but later reads still look at the stale path. Patch the resolver so successful re-resolution is retained for subsequent reads.\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/swe-style-entire-cli-transcript-reresolve.json:13:      \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/strategy/resolve_transcript.go\",\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/swe-style-entire-cli-transcript-reresolve.json:21:  \"expected_files\": [\"cmd/entire/cli/strategy/resolve_transcript.go\"],\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/swe-style-entire-cli-transcript-reresolve.json:23:  \"brain_queries\": [\"transcript re-resolution state update\", \"resolveTranscriptPath\"]\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/panels/release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-review-base-scope.json:2:  \"name\": \"release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-review-base-scope\",\nbenchmarks/agent-