{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:28:59.234Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<subagent_notification>\n{\"agent_path\":\"019eb218-2e2a-7a82-9d0c-49f4e4597681\",\"status\":{\"completed\":\"**Audit Result**\\nCurrent retained distill proof is valid but narrow. `mise run distill:evidence` passes at HEAD `46ba2d8`, proving only:\\n\\n- current-repo target: `github.com/ashtom/entire-brain`\\n- deterministic local `command` agent\\n- dry-run sizing plus paired `--jobs 1` / `--jobs 4` timing\\n- scheduler speedup: `18.28485225s / 9.160083208s = 1.996x`\\n- fake loopback Ollama wiring/no-egress contract: 9/9 required tests\\n\\nIt does not prove the `entire.io/frontend` 24h complaint is solved.\\n\\nI made one doc-only correction:\\n- [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:61) now says “retained measured head” instead of “current release-hardening head.”\\n\\nValidation:\\n- `git diff --check` passed\\n- `mise run distill:evidence` passed\\n\\n**What Is Proven**\\nThe retained manifest targets `github.com/ashtom/entire-brain`, not frontend: [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:3).\\n\\nThe retained dry-run reports 147 sessions, 159 chunks, 7,419,024 preprocessed bytes, and an upper bound of 318 agent calls: [dry-run.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/dry-run.json:11).\\n\\nThe retained timed runs show matching outputs and the speedup:\\n- `jobs-1.json`: 159 extraction calls, 136 reconcile calls, 18.28s: [jobs-1.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/jobs-1.json:24)\\n- `jobs-4.json`: same calls/output, 9.16s: [jobs-4.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/jobs-4.json:24)\\n\\nThe command-agent fixture is explicitly not model-quality proof: [local-command-agent.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/local-command-agent.py:2).\\n\\nOllama support is real at the contract level: loopback URL only, no proxy/TLS hook, non-streaming `/api/generate`, model required: [distill_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1361), with tests retained in the manifest: [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:76).\\n\\n**Remaining Gap**\\nFor a production-ready frontend claim, the missing evidence is target-specific:\\n\\n- dry-run JSON from the actual `entire.io/frontend` repo/brain\\n- paired timed `--jobs 1` and `--jobs N` JSON on the same target repo/cache state\\n- manifest target set to frontend repo, frontend source head, frontend brain manifest hash, and frontend-specific claim scope\\n- zero failed chunks/warnings\\n- matching serial/parallel output counts\\n- observed speedup above `min_speedup`\\n- optional but stronger: the same pair using real local Ollama, not just fake-Ollama contract tests\\n\\nThe docs already state this correctly: [release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:73), [distill-perf README](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/README.md:10).\\n\\n**Smallest Next Fixture**\\nNo code patch is required for the next stronger proof. The smallest production-relevant fixture is a retained frontend distill artifact set, using the existing audit:\\n\\n```sh\\nTARGET=/absolute/path/to/entire.io/frontend\\nEVID=benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf\\nJOBS_N=4\\n\\nentire-brain refresh \\\"$TARGET\\\"\\nBRAIN_DIR=\\\"$(entire-brain path \\\"$TARGET\\\")\\\"\\nSOURCE_HEAD=\\\"$(git -C \\\"$TARGET\\\" rev-parse HEAD)\\\"\\nBRAIN_SHA=\\\"sha256:$(shasum -a 256 \\\"$BRAIN_DIR/manifest.json\\\" | awk '{print $1}')\\\"\\n\\nentire-brain distill \\\"$TARGET\\\" --dry-run --json \\\\\\n  --agent command \\\\\\n  --agent-command python3 \\\\\\n  --agent-command benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/local-command-agent.py \\\\\\n  --force --max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75 --jobs 1 \\\\\\n  > \\\"$EVID/dry-run.json\\\"\\n\\n/usr/bin/time -p -o \\\"$EVID/jobs-1.time\\\" \\\\\\n  entire-brain distill \\\"$TARGET\\\" --json \\\\\\n  --agent command \\\\\\n  --agent-command python3 \\\\\\n  --agent-command benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/local-command-agent.py \\\\\\n  --force --max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75 --jobs 1 \\\\\\n  > \\\"$EVID/jobs-1.json\\\"\\n\\n/usr/bin/time -p -o \\\"$EVID/jobs-4.time\\\" \\\\\\n  entire-brain distill \\\"$TARGET\\\" --json \\\\\\n  --agent command \\\\\\n  --agent-command python3 \\\\\\n  --agent-command benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/local-command-agent.py \\\\\\n  --force --max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75 --jobs \\\"$JOBS_N\\\" \\\\\\n  > \\\"$EVID/jobs-4.json\\\"\\n\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py \\\\\\n  --manifest \\\"$EVID/manifest.json\\\" \\\\\\n  --out-dir \\\"$EVID\\\" \\\\\\n  --fail-on-flags\\n\\nmise run distill:evidence\\n```\\n\\nFor a local-model claim, repeat the paired timed runs with:\\n\\n```sh\\nENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS=1 \\\\\\nENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate \\\\\\nentire-brain distill \\\"$TARGET\\\" --json --agent ollama --model <local-model> ...\\n```\\n\\nUse the command-agent fixture first for target scheduler proof. Use real Ollama only if the release claim needs “frontend can be distilled locally with this model,” because that is the expensive evidence path.\"}}\n</subagent_notification>"}]}}
