{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:30:19.105Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_nWKhzB0Jfhba8mDSZFeRvGKC","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb15c-ebdd-7010-8d01-d3308a5d263e\":{\"completed\":\"No files changed. I only read files and ran checks. I avoided Radar/MCP files.\\n\\n**Conclusion**\\n\\nCurrent retained facts evidence is honest-negative/no-claim. A positive facts-vs-raw proof is **not production-ready** yet.\\n\\n**P0 Blockers**\\n\\n1. **No positive retained artifacts exist**\\n   - Manifest is explicitly no-claim and has no summaries, comparisons, or claims: [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/manifest.json:3).\\n   - Retained status has `facts_arm_ready: false`, `active: 0`, and no facts source: [facts-status.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/facts-status.json:6).\\n   - Live local status also reports zero facts on current branch and all branches.\\n   - Missing artifacts: `facts.json`, `history.json`, `query.json`, `raw-sessions.json`, `raw-vs-facts.compare.json`, proof manifest, regenerated audit reports, and ideally the exact proof-labeled task file.\\n\\n2. **Positive audit can still trust forged metric winner/significance**\\n   - The audit recomputes pairing and metric `n`, but still trusts comparison JSON for `winner`, `significant`, and `release_claimable`: [audit_facts_eval.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py:450).\\n   - Temp-only forged fixture proved this: retained rows had raw `useful_per_1k` greater than facts, but comparison JSON claimed facts won; audit returned `status: pass`, `claimable_facts_vs_raw: true`.\\n   - Existing positive fixture is hand-authored and does not include metric values in summary rows: [run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2732).\\n\\n**P1 Blockers**\\n\\n3. **The original proof-labeled task file is not required as retained evidence**\\n   - README says to use one immutable task file: [README.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/README.md:74).\\n   - But retained shape omits the task artifact itself: [README.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/README.md:24).\\n   - Summaries retain `tasks_sha256`, but not the original `relevant` IDs from the task file; those live in `evalTask`, not `evalTaskResult`: [facts_eval.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_eval.go:27), [facts_eval.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_eval.go:43).\\n\\n**Smallest Next Patch**\\n\\nPatch facts-eval only:\\n\\n1. Add a failing regression test in `FactsEvalAuditScriptTests` where retained summary metrics make raw better than facts, but compare JSON claims facts won/significant.\\n2. Update `audit_facts_eval.py` to verify known metric values from retained summaries before accepting a positive claim:\\n   - recompute `mean_a`, `mean_b`, `delta`, `winner`, and `n` for `precision`, `recall`, `useful_per_1k`, `tokens`, `latency_ms`;\\n   - for full rigor, either recompute significance/Holm in Python or regenerate `facts eval-compare --json` from retained summaries and compare against the retained comparison.\\n3. Add docs/manifest support requiring the proof task file artifact plus SHA match before positive proof mode.\\n\\n**Checks Run**\\n\\n- `mise run facts:evidence` passed as no-claim evidence.\\n- `python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py FactsEvalAuditScriptTests` passed.\\n- `go run ./cmd/entire-brain facts status --json` and `--all-branches` both reported zero facts.\\n- Temp-only forged positive fixture currently passes the audit, proving the remaining gate gap.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
