{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:34:50.239Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"thread_goal_updated","threadId":"019eacc8-4c81-7c91-b807-b3c82bbba45d","turnId":"49b267db-5c73-4329-a14f-bdafb54c36da","goal":{"threadId":"019eacc8-4c81-7c91-b807-b3c82bbba45d","objective":"now do it ; audit fully end to end; and fix ALL LOSE ends of the brain i know htsi might takes days; don't sotp until brain fully ifxed losed ends and fulyl aduit that that is the case ; use subagents etc; and make sure u finish thomas needs to th e mmaxium extent psosbiel; and do the full aduit ccle on it too end to end ; REQUIREMNTS; this is probraly should be read at around 256M tokens of usage; so yeha a lot of time; oh also IDC abt credits and cost so use fully infien sub agent tasks worflwos etc etc; finsih goal fully; should have abt 260k+ new lines of code etc; filling evyerhitng which is half made etc etc; at the end entire brain shoudl ebcoem full prodcution level relase with eveyrhting thomas wants , my token suage , my liens of code vaildaited end to end etc etc; spend all u can and go fast etc too","status":"active","tokensUsed":22857700,"timeUsedSeconds":83459,"createdAt":1781030922,"updatedAt":1781112890}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:34:50.271Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_pWPjpIZGNBpCtsjT0IrX2pJo","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb22a-8e82-7b11-a8f6-daf7ad5e5db4\":{\"completed\":\"No `Makefile` found; the actionable task surface is [mise.toml](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:6) plus the release/Radar docs. Also note the worktree is already dirty: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:488) has `44 -> 47` focused tests. I did not edit it.\\n\\n**Fastest Useful Sequence**\\n\\n1. **Current-code Radar/MCP contract smoke**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p go test ./internal/cli -run '^(TestRegression|TestInspectRegressions|TestMCP|TestWorkspaceRegressions)'\\n   ```\\n   Duration observed: ~2.6s for the retained 47-test regex; this broader regex should still be seconds.  \\n   Proves current branch code still passes the live MCP/Radar tests, not just the retained artifact.\\n\\n2. **Retained MCP/Radar tool evidence**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p mise run radar:evidence\\n   ```\\n   Duration observed: 0.17s, PASS.  \\n   Proves the committed deterministic MCP/Radar artifact is hash-valid and covers 47 required tests: location-only redaction, deletion opt-in, workspace Radar, strict MCP args, QMD MCP retrieval, and safe `tool_result` logging. This is citable tool-contract proof, not agent lift.\\n\\n3. **Thomas/Radar saturation screen**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p mise run radar:screen\\n   ```\\n   Duration observed: 0.25s.  \\n   Proves the Thomas question directly: whether Radar has real no-brain headroom or just saturation/audit gaps. Current result: 26 Radar comparisons, 0 proof-ready, 0 promotable; useful for deciding not to spend the next hour on saturated panels.\\n\\n4. **Retained replay-lab release evidence**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p mise run release:evidence\\n   ```\\n   Duration observed: 0.99s, PASS.  \\n   Proves retained release evidence is audit-clean for current manifest scopes: `history` and generic `mcp`. Current retained lane has 2 suites, 16 records, 4 MCP-verified records, 0 named/completed MCP tool records, so it supports generic MCP/history readiness but not Radar agent-lift.\\n\\n5. **Candidate task/panel preflight**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py check --tasks \\\\\\n     entireio-cli-radar-review-base-file-count.json \\\\\\n     entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions.json \\\\\\n     entireio-cli-manual-commit-attribution-base.json \\\\\\n     entireio-cli-transcript-reresolve.json\\n   ```\\n   Duration observed: ~20s, PASS.  \\n   Proves the committed Radar/MCP candidate tasks still fail as expected before agents run. This is high-signal and cheap before spending agent time.\\n\\n6. **Other retained claim gates**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p mise run distill:evidence\\n   /usr/bin/time -p mise run facts:evidence\\n   ```\\n   Durations observed: 0.16s and 0.12s, both PASS.  \\n   These are not Radar/MCP lift proof, but they keep release copy honest: distill has narrow scheduler-speed evidence; facts is explicit `no_release_claim`.\\n\\n7. **Semantic freshness gate, currently expected to fail**\\n   ```sh\\n   /usr/bin/time -p mise run semantic:evidence\\n   ```\\n   Duration observed: 1.08s, FAIL.  \\n   It reports `freshness=unsafe`, `head: stale`, `worktree: dirty-unindexed`. This is useful release-readiness signal, but do not burn time debugging Radar with this unless you are ready to refresh the local semantic index.\\n\\nI would not start with `mise run release:readiness` in a no-edit sidecar pass. It runs [check + all evidence gates](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:286), and `check` depends on lint tasks including `go mod tidy` via `lint:gomod`, which can modify `go.mod`/`go.sum`. For this next hour, the sequence above gives the best signal/time without touching files.\"},\"019eb218-4951-7fb1-9cac-97592b329318\":{\"completed\":\"**P0/P1 Blockers**\\n\\nNone found in the current branch for the QMD/MCP surface. The earlier blockers look fixed: MCP now calls/asserts `brain_query` alongside `brain_search`, `brain_vsearch`, `brain_get`, and `brain_multi_get` in [internal/cli/mcp_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:742), and `mcp_semantic` no longer presents `brain_query` as semantic graph search in [benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py:2105).\\n\\n**P2 Gaps**\\n\\n1. CLI `--branch` override behavior is still mostly advertised, not behaviorally pinned.  \\n   Flags are wired for all verbs in [internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:46) and passed through at [internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:61), but CLI tests seed the fake current branch and do not pass `--branch` ([internal/cli/retrieve_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_test.go:147)). MCP branch behavior is better covered.\\n\\n2. `get`/`multi-get` JSON does not include resolved `branch`, unlike search/query/vsearch.  \\n   Retrieval JSON includes `branch` at [internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:69), but `runGet` emits only `results` and `missing` at [internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:161). This is not necessarily wrong, but it weakens auditability for branch-scoped fetches.\\n\\n3. `--limit` / `-n` precedence is only pinned on `search`.  \\n   The implementation is shared in [internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:29), so risk is low, but `TestQMDLimitAliasesAndPrecedence` only exercises `search` ([internal/cli/retrieve_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_test.go:219)). `query`/`vsearch` get lighter alias coverage.\\n\\n4. MCP schema test could assert the full required-field contract, not just branch/minItems.  \\n   Schemas correctly set required fields via [internal/cli/mcp.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp.go:230), but the QMD schema test currently checks branch and `multi_get` `minItems` only ([internal/cli/mcp_test.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/mcp_test.go:116)).\\n\\n5. Release doc still says 48 focused tests while the retained Radar/QMD contract now has 49.  \\n   See [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:494) vs required test list starting at [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json:30).\\n\\n**Recommended Fixes**\\n\\nAdd one CLI branch-override table test covering `search`, `query`, `vsearch`, `get`, and `multi-get` with a non-current branch and wrong-branch negative case. Decide whether `get`/`multi-get` JSON should include `branch`; either add it and test it, or document the omission. Expand limit precedence over `query` and `vsearch`, and strengthen MCP schema assertions for `required` and `limit.minimum`.\\n\\nVerification: focused Go QMD/MCP tests passed. The two benchmark runner-policy tests passed with corrected invocation. No network, no edits, no PR/push.\"},\"019eb1c9-d797-73e1-a3cb-cd83ff65795d\":{\"completed\":\"At HEAD `46ba2d8`, `mise run radar:screen` still reports **27 Radar comparisons, 0 proof-ready**. I generated fresh read-only audit artifacts at `/var/folders/wb/5flrfjsj0px0nc4tvnbkxrhc0000gn/T/tmp.WNPFWkFRug`.\\n\\n**Not Proof-Ready**\\n\\n1. `...deletions-tool-result-rerun-20260610T122500Z`  \\n   The MCP evidence is good, but the Radar arm is not clean. The suite summary has `candidate_proof_ready: false`, `proof_ready: false`, pass-rate `0.25 -> 0.75`, and `verdict_reasons: brain_validation_not_clean`: [summary.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-tool-result-rerun-20260610T122500Z/summary.json:16), [summary.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-tool-result-rerun-20260610T122500Z/summary.json:64), [summary.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-tool-result-rerun-20260610T122500Z/summary.json:90).  \\n   The failed Radar rep is `mcp_history__r3`: `validation_passed: 1`, score `67`: [record.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-tool-result-rerun-20260610T122500Z/entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions__codex-gpt-5.4-mini-low__mcp_history__r3/record.json:478). Server proof is present (`tool`, safe args, `tool_result`): [mcp-server.log](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-tool-result-rerun-20260610T122500Z/entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions__codex-gpt-5.4-mini-low__mcp_history__r1/mcp-server.log:9).  \\n   Audit says `4/4` named/completed overall, but only **3** clean condition records where **4** are required: [codex-audit-report.json](/var/folders/wb/5flrfjsj0px0nc4tvnbkxrhc0000gn/T/tmp.WNPFWkFRug/codex-audit-report.json:6063).\\n\\n2. `...deletions-tool-result-20260610T115718Z`  \\n   Same shape: good MCP proof, bad clean pass-rate. Summary says `candidate_proof_ready: false`, `proof_ready: false`, pass-rate `0.00 -> 0.75`, `brain_validation_not_clean`: [summary.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-tool-result-20260610T115718Z/summary.json:16), [summary.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-tool-result-20260610T115718Z/summary.json:64), [summary.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-tool-result-20260610T115718Z/summary.json:90).  \\n   The failed Radar rep is `mcp_history__r2`: `validation_passed: 1`, score `69`: [record.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-tool-result-20260610T115718Z/entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions__codex-gpt-5.4-mini-low__mcp_history__r2/record.json:478). Audit backing again has only **3** clean condition records vs required **4**: [codex-audit-report.json](/var/folders/wb/5flrfjsj0px0nc4tvnbkxrhc0000gn/T/tmp.WNPFWkFRug/codex-audit-report.json:5556).\\n\\n3. `...deletions-all-loci-rerun-20260610Tprogress`  \\n   This is statistically the strongest, but the MCP proof binding is old/incomplete. Summary says `candidate_proof_ready: true`, `proof_ready: true`, pass-rate `0.25 -> 1.00`, `verdict: brain_positive`: [summary.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-all-loci-rerun-20260610Tprogress/summary.json:16), [summary.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-all-loci-rerun-20260610Tprogress/summary.json:64), [summary.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-all-loci-rerun-20260610Tprogress/summary.json:90).  \\n   But server logs only show `tool: brain_regressions`; they lack `tool_args` and `tool_result`: [mcp-server.log](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-all-loci-rerun-20260610Tprogress/entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions__codex-gpt-5.4-mini-low__mcp_history__r1/mcp-server.log:8). The record also lacks `task.radar_include_deletions`; compare absence after task path here: [record.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/results/release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-all-loci-rerun-20260610Tprogress/entireio-cli-radar-manual-attribution-deletions__codex-gpt-5.4-mini-low__mcp_history__r1/record.json:397).  \\n   Audit flags all four Radar records with `H:provenance_missing_radar_include_deletions_policy`, `B:mcp_radar_server_missing_location_only`, and `B:mcp_required_tool_results_missing(brain_regressions)`: [codex-audit-report.md](/var/folders/wb/5flrfjsj0px0nc4tvnbkxrhc0000gn/T/tmp.WNPFWkFRug/codex-audit-report.md:110). The comparison then gets `G:proof_ready_without_*` flags: [codex-audit-report.md](/var/folders/wb/5flrfjsj0px0nc4tvnbkxrhc0000gn/T/tmp.WNPFWkFRug/codex-audit-report.md:114).\\n\\n**Smallest Honest Path**\\n\\nDo **not** fix the auditor or promote the manifest from these artifacts. The auditor is catching real gaps: either unclean Radar reps or missing server/provenance proof.\\n\\nSmallest honest path is a fresh rerun of the existing deletion panel at current HEAD, then promote only if it has both clean lift and named/result-backed MCP proof:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py panel \\\\\\n  release-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions \\\\\\n  --suite-name release-candidate-entire-cli-radar-mcp-manual-attribution-deletions-tool-result-current-20260610TXXXXZ\\n```\\n\\nThen audit that suite with `audit_codex.py` plus `audit_radar_evidence.py --fail-when-no-proof`. If it gets 4 clean Radar condition records, server `tool_args` with `location_only/include_deletions`, `tool_result`, and non-saturated pass-rate lift, then retain it and update the release manifest.\"},\"019eb1c9-da6e-7553-a01e-d6837efa84a3\":{\"completed\":\"Implemented the smallest offline retained-evidence improvement: the distill evidence now retains and audits a fake loopback Ollama contract artifact, without needing a real model.\\n\\nKey files:\\n- [audit_distill_perf.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py:16): requires exact Ollama distill source paths, 9 focused tests, and `go test -count=1 -json`.\\n- [audit_distill_perf.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py:154): validates artifact hash, command, source head, source paths, package pass, and required test pass events.\\n- [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:76): adds `local_ollama_contract` with retained artifact/hash/source/command/tests.\\n- [go-test-internal-cli-ollama-distill.jsonl](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/go-test-internal-cli-ollama-distill.jsonl): retained non-cached fake-Ollama `go test -json` proof.\\n- [run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2965): adds fixture coverage and failure tests for missing/failed Ollama contract evidence.\\n- [README.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/README.md:32) and [release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:33): document the claim boundary.\\n\\nVerified at current clean HEAD `abb0728`:\\n- `mise run distill:evidence`\\n- `python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py DistillPerfAuditScriptTests`\\n- `go test -count=1 ./internal/cli -run 'Test(DistillCommandOllamaLoopbackProducesTimedSummary|ExecOllamaDistillAgentUsesLoopbackGenerateAPI|ExecOllamaDistillAgentIgnoresProxyTransport|ExecOllamaDistillAgentIgnoresCustomTLSDialHook|ExecOllamaDistillAgentRejectsNonLoopbackURL|ExecOllamaDistillAgentRejectsNonLoopbackRedirect|IsLoopbackHTTPURLAllowsFullLoopbackRange|LoopbackOnlyDialContextRejectsNonLoopbackTargets|LoopbackOnlyDialContextAllowsLocalhostResolution)$'`\\n\\nNo PR or push. The evidence now supports “local Ollama wiring/no-egress works offline”; it still does not claim real Ollama model quality or target large-repo/frontend distill speed.\"},\"019eb15c-ebdd-7010-8d01-d3308a5d263e\":{\"completed\":\"No positive facts-vs-raw proof can be honestly produced from the current local/retained artifacts at `46ba2d8`. The gate is now hardened, but the evidence corpus is still explicitly **no-claim**.\\n\\n**P0 Blockers**\\n\\n1. **Facts arm is empty locally and in retained evidence**\\n   - Retained manifest is `claim_policy: \\\"no_release_claim\\\"` with empty `summaries`, `comparisons`, and `required_claims`: [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/manifest.json:3).\\n   - Retained status has `facts_arm_ready: false`, `active: 0`, and “no active facts”: [facts-status.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/facts-status.json:6).\\n   - Live check agrees: `go run ./cmd/entire-brain facts status --json --all-branches` reported `facts=0 active=0`.\\n   - Smallest close: create/retain active durable facts for the target branch first. Until `facts status --json` says `facts_arm_ready: true`, any facts-vs-raw win would be fiction.\\n\\n2. **No positive eval artifacts are retained**\\n   - Required retained shape is four summaries plus compare JSON plus required facts-beats-raw claim: [README.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/README.md:13).\\n   - Current directory contains only README, no-claim manifest, status, and no-claim audit reports; no `facts.json`, `history.json`, `query.json`, `raw-sessions.json`, or `raw-vs-facts.compare.json`.\\n   - Docs correctly say paired facts evals are still required: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:149), [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:611).\\n   - Smallest close: run the same immutable proof-labeled task file through `facts`, `history`, `query`, and `raw-sessions`; retain the four `facts eval --json` summaries and `facts eval-compare --json` for raw-vs-facts.\\n\\n**P1 Blockers**\\n\\n3. **Proof labels must be real, not source-match smoke**\\n   - CLI docs say source-session labels are proxy/smoke unless judged/refined: [facts_eval.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_eval.go:353).\\n   - `eval-compare` rejects non-proof relevance sources unless proxy mode is explicitly enabled: [facts_eval_compare.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_eval_compare.go:405).\\n   - Auditor requires proof labels and rejects proxy promotion: [audit_facts_eval.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py:436).\\n   - Smallest close: use human or `judge_refined` labels on the task set; do not use `--allow-proxy-comparison` for release proof.\\n\\n4. **The proof manifest/report must replace the no-claim manifest**\\n   - `mise run facts:evidence` only validates committed reports and fails if stale: [mise.toml](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:160).\\n   - Proof mode requires canonical retrievers, matching hashes, no missing IDs, claimable/significant metric, and facts beating raw: [audit_facts_eval.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py:298), [audit_facts_eval.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py:469).\\n   - Smallest close: replace `manifest.json` with proof-required entries, run `mise run facts:evidence:update`, then `mise run facts:evidence`.\\n\\nChecks run:\\n- `mise run facts:evidence` passed as no-claim evidence.\\n- `go run ./cmd/entire-brain facts status --json` and `--all-branches` both showed zero facts.\\n- `python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py FactsEvalAuditScriptTests` passed.\\n- `go test ./internal/cli -run 'Test.*(FactsEval|CompareEval|FactsStatus)' -count=1` passed.\"},\"019eb218-2e2a-7a82-9d0c-49f4e4597681\":{\"completed\":\"**Bottom Line**\\nAt HEAD `46ba2d8`, distill release readiness is stronger, but it still does **not** answer Thomas’s exact complaint: “24h distill on `entire.io/frontend`.” What is proven is current-repo scheduler/evidence-gate behavior plus fake loopback Ollama safety, not frontend-scale runtime or real local-model fact quality.\\n\\n**Proven Now**\\n- Dry-run sizing exists and is retained: current artifact reports 147 sessions, 159 chunks, 7,419,024 preprocessed bytes, and an upper bound of 318 agent calls in [dry-run.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/dry-run.json:11).\\n- Paired `--jobs` timing is retained: `--jobs 1` took `18.28485225s`; `--jobs 4` took `9.160083208s`, a `1.996x` speedup in [distill-perf-audit-report.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/distill-perf-audit-report.json:13).\\n- Timing fields are real summary fields: `extraction_seconds`, `reconcile_seconds`, `write_seconds`, and `total_seconds` are part of `sources.facts` in [facts.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts.go:70), populated in [distill_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:639).\\n- `--jobs N` parallelizes extraction only; reconciliation/writes stay deterministic per docs and implementation in [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:28) and [distill_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:934).\\n- Ollama/local model wiring exists and is retained as a contract: loopback `/api/generate`, no proxy/custom TLS hook, non-loopback rejection, and 9/9 required tests passing in [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:76) and [distill-perf-audit-report.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/distill-perf-audit-report.json:34).\\n- `mise run distill:evidence` passes at HEAD `46ba2d8`.\\n\\n**Still Missing**\\n- The retained target is `github.com/ashtom/entire-brain`, not `entire.io/frontend`, in [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:4).\\n- The manifest’s claim scope is only `current-repo local command-agent distill extraction scheduling speedup` in [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:8).\\n- The evidence README explicitly says these artifacts must not support the frontend/24h claim in [README.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/README.md:10).\\n- There is no retained frontend dry-run, no frontend `--jobs 1`/`--jobs N` pair, no frontend cache-state proof, and no real Ollama model timing on that repo.\\n- Minor doc staleness: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:60) says “current release-hardening head,” but the retained target source head is `55518db...`, not current `46ba2d8`.\\n\\n**Smallest Next Proof**\\nUse the existing audit path; no code changes are required for a stronger **frontend scheduler** proof. Stage local-only artifacts like this:\\n\\n```sh\\nTARGET=/absolute/path/to/entire.io/frontend\\nEVID=benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf\\nJOBS_N=4\\n\\nentire-brain refresh \\\"$TARGET\\\"\\nBRAIN=\\\"$(entire-brain path \\\"$TARGET\\\")\\\"\\nSOURCE_HEAD=\\\"$(git -C \\\"$TARGET\\\" rev-parse HEAD)\\\"\\nBRAIN_SHA=\\\"sha256:$(shasum -a 256 \\\"$BRAIN/manifest.json\\\" | awk '{print $1}')\\\"\\n\\nentire-brain distill \\\"$TARGET\\\" --dry-run --json \\\\\\n  --agent command \\\\\\n  --agent-command python3 \\\\\\n  --agent-command benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/local-command-agent.py \\\\\\n  --force --max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75 --jobs 1 \\\\\\n  > \\\"$EVID/dry-run.json\\\"\\n\\n/usr/bin/time -p -o \\\"$EVID/jobs-1.time\\\" \\\\\\nentire-brain distill \\\"$TARGET\\\" --json \\\\\\n  --agent command \\\\\\n  --agent-command python3 \\\\\\n  --agent-command benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/local-command-agent.py \\\\\\n  --force --max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75 --jobs 1 \\\\\\n  > \\\"$EVID/jobs-1.json\\\"\\n\\n/usr/bin/time -p -o \\\"$EVID/jobs-$JOBS_N.time\\\" \\\\\\nentire-brain distill \\\"$TARGET\\\" --json \\\\\\n  --agent command \\\\\\n  --agent-command python3 \\\\\\n  --agent-command benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/local-command-agent.py \\\\\\n  --force --max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75 --jobs \\\"$JOBS_N\\\" \\\\\\n  > \\\"$EVID/jobs-4.json\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThen update `manifest.json` to target `entire.io/frontend`, set `source_head=$SOURCE_HEAD`, `brain_manifest_sha256=$BRAIN_SHA`, and set claim scope to something narrow like `frontend local command-agent distill extraction scheduling speedup`. Regenerate/check:\\n\\n```sh\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py \\\\\\n  --manifest benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json \\\\\\n  --out-dir benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf \\\\\\n  --fail-on-flags\\n\\nmise run distill:evidence\\n```\\n\\nFor a stronger **local Ollama** proof, repeat the same paired run with:\\n\\n```sh\\nENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS=1 \\\\\\nENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate \\\\\\nentire-brain distill \\\"$TARGET\\\" --json --agent ollama --model <local-model> \\\\\\n  --force --max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75 --jobs \\\"$JOBS_N\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThat would support a frontend local-model timing claim only if the full target run is retained and audited; the current fake-Ollama artifact only proves wiring/no-egress safety.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
