{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:35:40.255Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_QhYYTnGEuMhNq218CYYa4Giy","output":"{\"status\":{\"completed\":\"No positive facts-vs-raw proof can be honestly produced from the current local/retained artifacts at `46ba2d8`. The gate is now hardened, but the evidence corpus is still explicitly **no-claim**.\\n\\n**P0 Blockers**\\n\\n1. **Facts arm is empty locally and in retained evidence**\\n   - Retained manifest is `claim_policy: \\\"no_release_claim\\\"` with empty `summaries`, `comparisons`, and `required_claims`: [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/manifest.json:3).\\n   - Retained status has `facts_arm_ready: false`, `active: 0`, and “no active facts”: [facts-status.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/facts-status.json:6).\\n   - Live check agrees: `go run ./cmd/entire-brain facts status --json --all-branches` reported `facts=0 active=0`.\\n   - Smallest close: create/retain active durable facts for the target branch first. Until `facts status --json` says `facts_arm_ready: true`, any facts-vs-raw win would be fiction.\\n\\n2. **No positive eval artifacts are retained**\\n   - Required retained shape is four summaries plus compare JSON plus required facts-beats-raw claim: [README.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/README.md:13).\\n   - Current directory contains only README, no-claim manifest, status, and no-claim audit reports; no `facts.json`, `history.json`, `query.json`, `raw-sessions.json`, or `raw-vs-facts.compare.json`.\\n   - Docs correctly say paired facts evals are still required: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:149), [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:611).\\n   - Smallest close: run the same immutable proof-labeled task file through `facts`, `history`, `query`, and `raw-sessions`; retain the four `facts eval --json` summaries and `facts eval-compare --json` for raw-vs-facts.\\n\\n**P1 Blockers**\\n\\n3. **Proof labels must be real, not source-match smoke**\\n   - CLI docs say source-session labels are proxy/smoke unless judged/refined: [facts_eval.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_eval.go:353).\\n   - `eval-compare` rejects non-proof relevance sources unless proxy mode is explicitly enabled: [facts_eval_compare.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_eval_compare.go:405).\\n   - Auditor requires proof labels and rejects proxy promotion: [audit_facts_eval.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py:436).\\n   - Smallest close: use human or `judge_refined` labels on the task set; do not use `--allow-proxy-comparison` for release proof.\\n\\n4. **The proof manifest/report must replace the no-claim manifest**\\n   - `mise run facts:evidence` only validates committed reports and fails if stale: [mise.toml](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:160).\\n   - Proof mode requires canonical retrievers, matching hashes, no missing IDs, claimable/significant metric, and facts beating raw: [audit_facts_eval.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py:298), [audit_facts_eval.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py:469).\\n   - Smallest close: replace `manifest.json` with proof-required entries, run `mise run facts:evidence:update`, then `mise run facts:evidence`.\\n\\nChecks run:\\n- `mise run facts:evidence` passed as no-claim evidence.\\n- `go run ./cmd/entire-brain facts status --json` and `--all-branches` both showed zero facts.\\n- `python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py FactsEvalAuditScriptTests` passed.\\n- `go test ./internal/cli -run 'Test.*(FactsEval|CompareEval|FactsStatus)' -count=1` passed.\"}}"}}
