{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:35:46.638Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_dB7vofmjxzkbCrSv6l4eGeI9","output":"{\"status\":{\"completed\":\"**Bottom Line**\\nAt HEAD `46ba2d8`, distill release readiness is stronger, but it still does **not** answer Thomas’s exact complaint: “24h distill on `entire.io/frontend`.” What is proven is current-repo scheduler/evidence-gate behavior plus fake loopback Ollama safety, not frontend-scale runtime or real local-model fact quality.\\n\\n**Proven Now**\\n- Dry-run sizing exists and is retained: current artifact reports 147 sessions, 159 chunks, 7,419,024 preprocessed bytes, and an upper bound of 318 agent calls in [dry-run.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/dry-run.json:11).\\n- Paired `--jobs` timing is retained: `--jobs 1` took `18.28485225s`; `--jobs 4` took `9.160083208s`, a `1.996x` speedup in [distill-perf-audit-report.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/distill-perf-audit-report.json:13).\\n- Timing fields are real summary fields: `extraction_seconds`, `reconcile_seconds`, `write_seconds`, and `total_seconds` are part of `sources.facts` in [facts.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts.go:70), populated in [distill_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:639).\\n- `--jobs N` parallelizes extraction only; reconciliation/writes stay deterministic per docs and implementation in [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:28) and [distill_cmd.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:934).\\n- Ollama/local model wiring exists and is retained as a contract: loopback `/api/generate`, no proxy/custom TLS hook, non-loopback rejection, and 9/9 required tests passing in [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:76) and [distill-perf-audit-report.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/distill-perf-audit-report.json:34).\\n- `mise run distill:evidence` passes at HEAD `46ba2d8`.\\n\\n**Still Missing**\\n- The retained target is `github.com/ashtom/entire-brain`, not `entire.io/frontend`, in [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:4).\\n- The manifest’s claim scope is only `current-repo local command-agent distill extraction scheduling speedup` in [manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:8).\\n- The evidence README explicitly says these artifacts must not support the frontend/24h claim in [README.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/README.md:10).\\n- There is no retained frontend dry-run, no frontend `--jobs 1`/`--jobs N` pair, no frontend cache-state proof, and no real Ollama model timing on that repo.\\n- Minor doc staleness: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:60) says “current release-hardening head,” but the retained target source head is `55518db...`, not current `46ba2d8`.\\n\\n**Smallest Next Proof**\\nUse the existing audit path; no code changes are required for a stronger **frontend scheduler** proof. Stage local-only artifacts like this:\\n\\n```sh\\nTARGET=/absolute/path/to/entire.io/frontend\\nEVID=benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf\\nJOBS_N=4\\n\\nentire-brain refresh \\\"$TARGET\\\"\\nBRAIN=\\\"$(entire-brain path \\\"$TARGET\\\")\\\"\\nSOURCE_HEAD=\\\"$(git -C \\\"$TARGET\\\" rev-parse HEAD)\\\"\\nBRAIN_SHA=\\\"sha256:$(shasum -a 256 \\\"$BRAIN/manifest.json\\\" | awk '{print $1}')\\\"\\n\\nentire-brain distill \\\"$TARGET\\\" --dry-run --json \\\\\\n  --agent command \\\\\\n  --agent-command python3 \\\\\\n  --agent-command benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/local-command-agent.py \\\\\\n  --force --max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75 --jobs 1 \\\\\\n  > \\\"$EVID/dry-run.json\\\"\\n\\n/usr/bin/time -p -o \\\"$EVID/jobs-1.time\\\" \\\\\\nentire-brain distill \\\"$TARGET\\\" --json \\\\\\n  --agent command \\\\\\n  --agent-command python3 \\\\\\n  --agent-command benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/local-command-agent.py \\\\\\n  --force --max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75 --jobs 1 \\\\\\n  > \\\"$EVID/jobs-1.json\\\"\\n\\n/usr/bin/time -p -o \\\"$EVID/jobs-$JOBS_N.time\\\" \\\\\\nentire-brain distill \\\"$TARGET\\\" --json \\\\\\n  --agent command \\\\\\n  --agent-command python3 \\\\\\n  --agent-command benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/local-command-agent.py \\\\\\n  --force --max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75 --jobs \\\"$JOBS_N\\\" \\\\\\n  > \\\"$EVID/jobs-4.json\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThen update `manifest.json` to target `entire.io/frontend`, set `source_head=$SOURCE_HEAD`, `brain_manifest_sha256=$BRAIN_SHA`, and set claim scope to something narrow like `frontend local command-agent distill extraction scheduling speedup`. Regenerate/check:\\n\\n```sh\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py \\\\\\n  --manifest benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json \\\\\\n  --out-dir benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf \\\\\\n  --fail-on-flags\\n\\nmise run distill:evidence\\n```\\n\\nFor a stronger **local Ollama** proof, repeat the same paired run with:\\n\\n```sh\\nENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS=1 \\\\\\nENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate \\\\\\nentire-brain distill \\\"$TARGET\\\" --json --agent ollama --model <local-model> \\\\\\n  --force --max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75 --jobs \\\"$JOBS_N\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThat would support a frontend local-model timing claim only if the full target run is retained and audited; the current fake-Ollama artifact only proves wiring/no-egress safety.\"}}"}}
