{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:38:48.639Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_doPNmAgKE73H8wcDUs0BBCds","output":"{\"status\":{\"019eb15c-ebdd-7010-8d01-d3308a5d263e\":{\"completed\":\"**Bottom Line**\\n\\nSynthetic proof-labeled fixtures in repo tests are enough to prove the **facts-eval gate works**, but not enough to honestly unblock a **release-citable facts-vs-raw win**. For that, you need real local session-derived facts plus retained eval artifacts from `facts eval`/`eval-compare`.\\n\\nCurrent local truth: `facts status --json` and `--all-branches` both report `facts=0 active=0`, matching the retained no-claim evidence.\\n\\n**What Exists**\\n\\n- Synthetic positive gate fixture: [benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py:2733)\\n- Current retained evidence is explicitly no-claim: [benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/manifest.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/manifest.json:3)\\n- Current retained status says zero active facts: [facts-status.json](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/facts-status.json:6)\\n- Docs correctly say positive proof is still blocked: [docs/release_readiness_audit.md](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md:149)\\n\\n**Key Constraint**\\n\\nA raw-vs-facts proof task cannot just list `fact:` IDs. `facts eval` filters relevant IDs by retriever: `fact:` for facts, `raw:` for raw sessions, `history:` for history, etc. See [facts_eval.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_eval.go:862). So an honest proof task needs human/judge-refined labels for the item IDs each cited arm can surface.\\n\\n**Smallest Honest Evidence Path**\\n\\n1. Build real local facts from real local sessions.\\n\\n```bash\\ngo run ./cmd/entire-brain refresh sessions\\ngo run ./cmd/entire-brain distill --branch codex/release-readiness-hardening --agent <agent> --model <model> --jobs 4 --json > /tmp/facts-proof/distill.json\\ngo run ./cmd/entire-brain facts status --json > /tmp/facts-proof/facts-status.json\\n```\\n\\n2. Generate a candidate task set from real fact provenance, then refine it.\\n\\n```bash\\ngo run ./cmd/entire-brain facts eval-gen \\\\\\n  --branch codex/release-readiness-hardening \\\\\\n  --min-facts 1 \\\\\\n  --max-facts 5 \\\\\\n  --limit 12 \\\\\\n  --refine \\\\\\n  --agent <agent> \\\\\\n  --model <model> \\\\\\n  --judge-cache /tmp/facts-proof/refine-cache.json \\\\\\n  --out /tmp/facts-proof/tasks.fact-labels.json\\n```\\n\\n`--refine` produces `judge_refined` labels: [facts_eval_gen.go](/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_eval_gen.go:126).\\n\\n3. Discover raw-session item IDs, then human-review the task labels.\\n\\n```bash\\ngo run ./cmd/entire-brain facts eval \\\\\\n  --tasks /tmp/facts-proof/tasks.fact-labels.json \\\\\\n  --retriever raw-sessions \\\\\\n  --json > /tmp/facts-proof/raw-sessions.discovery.json\\n```\\n\\nCreate `/tmp/facts-proof/tasks.proof.json` by retaining the relevant `fact:` IDs and adding relevant `raw:` IDs for each task, with `label_source: \\\"human\\\"` or `\\\"judge_refined\\\"`.\\n\\n4. Run all four canonical arms on the same final task file.\\n\\n```bash\\nfor arm in facts history query raw-sessions; do\\n  go run ./cmd/entire-brain facts eval \\\\\\n    --tasks /tmp/facts-proof/tasks.proof.json \\\\\\n    --retriever \\\"$arm\\\" \\\\\\n    --json > \\\"/tmp/facts-proof/$arm.json\\\"\\ndone\\n```\\n\\n5. Compare raw vs facts.\\n\\n```bash\\ngo run ./cmd/entire-brain facts eval-compare \\\\\\n  --a /tmp/facts-proof/raw-sessions.json \\\\\\n  --b /tmp/facts-proof/facts.json \\\\\\n  --json > /tmp/facts-proof/raw-vs-facts.compare.json\\n```\\n\\nOnly proceed if the cited metric has `winner: \\\"b\\\"`, `evidence_basis: \\\"proof_labels\\\"`, `significant: true`, and `release_claimable: true`.\\n\\n6. Retain artifacts under `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/`:\\n- `tasks.proof.json`\\n- `facts-status.json`\\n- `facts.json`\\n- `history.json`\\n- `query.json`\\n- `raw-sessions.json`\\n- `raw-vs-facts.compare.json`\\n- updated `manifest.json`\\n- regenerated `facts-eval-audit-report.{json,md}`\\n\\nThen run:\\n\\n```bash\\nmise run facts:evidence:update\\nmise run facts:evidence\\n```\\n\\n**Implementation Note**\\n\\nNo product-code change is required for collection. The one worthwhile small hardening patch would be to make `audit_facts_eval.py` require the retained `tasks.proof.json` path/hash in positive proof manifests. Right now the summaries carry `tasks_sha256`, but the task file itself is not required by the auditor. That is not a blocker to running the evidence, but it is the cleanest next honesty guard.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}"}}
