{"timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:39:27.593Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","turn_id":"73af0e13-622c-47d4-b956-79de5e9fdbdf","last_agent_message":"Finished the current slice and opened the PR.\n\nPR: https://github.com/ashtom/entire-brain/pull/32  \nCommit: `c0d93b6 Harden release evidence audits`\n\nWhat changed:\n- Facts-vs-raw audit now recomputes retained row `mean_a`, `mean_b`, `delta`, and `winner` before accepting a positive claim.\n- Added forged-winner regression coverage.\n- Tightened MCP audit arg sanitization so `workspace` is only safe for workspace tools.\n- Clarified retained distill evidence wording.\n\nValidation passed locally:\n- `python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py FactsEvalAuditScriptTests CodexAuditScriptTests`\n- `python3 -m py_compile ...`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `mise run facts:evidence`\n- `mise run radar:evidence`\n- `mise run release:evidence`\n\nPR status:\n- Mergeable.\n- Retargeted as a stacked PR against `codex/release-readiness-base`, because the full branch against `main` has 134 pending release-readiness commits and broad conflicts.\n- GitHub completed checks are green so far; two Windows jobs were still running when I stopped.\n\nLocal uncommitted files are only tool/config state: `.claude`, `.codex`, `.cursor`, `.gemini`, `.mcp.json`, `.regente`.","completed_at":1781113167,"duration_ms":592624,"time_to_first_token_ms":10317}}
